  (23792, 124, '(Applause)', 414.699, 418.247, NULL),
  (23793, 124, 'Thank you.', 418.247, 419.436, NULL),
  (23794, 124, 'So the bottom line here,', 419.436, 421.395, NULL),
  (23795, 124, 'is that I hope you appreciate
and love your family,', 421.395, 425.294, NULL),
  (23796, 124, 'love your friends,
for you guys, love you Bro’s', 425.294, 428.453, NULL),
  (23797, 124, 'and acknowledge your mentors,', 428.453, 431.860, NULL),
  (23798, 124, 'and your community,', 431.860, 433.557, NULL),
  (23799, 124, 'because they are a very real
aspect of everyday life,', 433.557, 436.654, NULL),
  (23800, 124, 'they can make a truly significant,
positive impact.', 436.654, 440.980, NULL),
  (23801, 124, 'The third aspect to the philosophy is,', 440.980, 443.663, NULL),
  (23802, 124, 'Keep moving forward.', 443.663, 445.898, NULL),
  (23803, 124, 'Here’s a quote by a man
you may know, named Walt Disney,', 445.898, 449.686, NULL),
  (23804, 124, 'and it’s one of my favorite quotes.', 449.686, 451.495, NULL),
  (23805, 124, 'I always try to have something
to look forward to.', 451.495, 454.230, NULL),
  (23806, 124, 'Something to strive for
to make my life richer.', 454.230, 457.265, NULL),
  (23807, 124, 'It doesn’t have to be big.', 457.265, 458.956, NULL),
  (23808, 124, 'It could be anything from', 458.956, 461.339, NULL),
  (23809, 124, 'looking forward to
the next comic book to come out,', 461.339, 463.946, NULL),
  (23810, 124, 'or going on a large family vacation,', 463.946, 466.467, NULL),
  (23811, 124, 'or hanging out with my friends,', 466.467, 468.736, NULL),
  (23812, 124, 'to going to the next
High School football game.', 468.736, 471.691, NULL),
  (23813, 124, 'However, all of these things
keep me focused,', 471.691, 475.013, NULL),
  (23814, 124, 'and know that there’s
a bright future ahead,', 475.013, 477.851, NULL),
  (23815, 124, 'and may get me through
some difficult times that I may be having.', 477.851, 482.287, NULL),
  (23816, 124, 'Now this mentality includes staying
in a forward thinking state of mind.', 482.287, 487.795, NULL),
  (23817, 124, 'I try hard not to waste energy
feeling badly for myself,', 487.795, 491.389, NULL),
  (23818, 124, 'because when I do,
I get stuck in a paradox,', 491.389, 494.871, NULL),
  (23819, 124, 'where there’s no room for 
any happiness or any other emotion.', 494.871, 499.454, NULL),
  (23820, 124, 'Now, it’s not that I ignore
when I’m feeling badly,', 499.454, 503.015, NULL),
  (23821, 124, 'I kind of accept it,', 503.015, 504.897, NULL),
  (23822, 124, 'I let it in, 
so that I can acknowledge it,', 504.897, 508.273, NULL),
  (23823, 124, 'and do what I need to do 
to move past it.', 508.273, 511.775, NULL),
  (23824, 124, 'When I was younger,
I wanted to be an engineer.', 511.775, 515.081, NULL),
  (23825, 124, 'I wanted to be an inventor,', 515.081, 516.995, NULL),
  (23826, 124, 'who would catapult the world
into a better future.', 516.995, 520.009, NULL),
  (23827, 124, 'Maybe this came 
from my love of Legos,', 520.009, 522.184, NULL),
  (23828, 124, 'and the freedom of expression 
that I felt', 522.184, 524.502, NULL),
  (23829, 124, 'when I was building with them.', 524.502, 527.814, NULL),
  (23830, 124, 'And this was also derived
from my family and my mentors,', 527.814, 533.489, NULL),
  (23831, 124, 'who always make me feel whole,
and good about myself.', 533.489, 537.985, NULL),
  (23832, 124, 'Now today my ambitions
have changed a little bit,', 537.985, 541.133, NULL),
  (23833, 124, 'I’d like to go into the field of Biology,', 541.133, 543.609, NULL),
  (23834, 124, 'maybe cell biology, or genetics,', 543.609, 547.948, NULL),
  (23835, 124, 'or biochemistry, or really anything.', 547.948, 552.417, NULL),
  (23836, 124, 'This is a friend of mine,
who I look up to,', 552.417, 555.698, NULL),
  (23837, 124, 'Francis Collins, the director of the NIH,', 555.698, 559.252, NULL),
  (23838, 124, 'and this is us at TEDMED last year,
chatting away.', 559.252, 562.670, NULL),
  (23839, 124, 'I feel that no matter what
I choose to become,', 562.670, 566.208, NULL),
  (23840, 124, 'I believe that I can change the world.', 566.208, 569.521, NULL),
  (23841, 124, 'And as I’m striving to change the world,
I will be happy.', 569.521, 574.417, NULL),
  (23842, 124, 'About four years ago,', 574.417, 576.562, NULL),
  (23843, 124, 'HBO began to film a documentary', 576.562, 579.247, NULL),
  (23844, 124, 'about my family and me
called “Life According to Sam”.', 579.247, 582.282, NULL),
  (23845, 124, 'That was a pretty great experience,
but it was also four years ago.', 582.282, 586.285, NULL),
  (23846, 124, 'And like anyone, my views
on many things have changed,', 586.285, 589.761, NULL),
  (23847, 124, 'and hopefully matured,
like my potential career choice.', 589.761, 594.165, NULL),
  (23848, 124, 'However, some things have stayed 
the same throughout that time.', 594.165, 598.798, NULL),
  (23849, 124, 'Like my mentality,
and philosophy towards life.', 598.798, 602.679, NULL),
  (23850, 124, 'So I would like to show you', 602.679, 604.730, NULL),
  (23851, 124, 'a clip of my younger self from the film,', 604.730, 607.921, NULL),
  (23852, 124, 'that I feel embodies that philosophy.', 607.921, 611.492, NULL),
  (23853, 124, '(Video)', 611.492, 612.659, NULL),
  (23854, 124, 'I know more about it genetically.', 612.659, 616.314, NULL),
  (23855, 124, 'So it’s less of an embodiment now.', 616.314, 619.857, NULL),
  (23856, 124, 'It used to be like', 619.857, 621.335, NULL),
  (23857, 124, 'this thing that prevents me
from doing all this stuff,', 621.335, 624.135, NULL),
  (23858, 124, 'that causes other kids to die,', 624.135, 626.669, NULL),
  (23859, 124, 'that causes everybody 
to be stressed,', 626.669, 629.639, NULL),
  (23860, 124, 'and now
it’s a protein that is abnormal,', 629.639, 635.276, NULL),
  (23861, 124, 'that weakens the structure of cells.', 635.276, 639.072, NULL),
  (23862, 124, 'So,', 640.465, 642.076, NULL),
  (23863, 124, 'and it takes a burden
off of me because now', 642.076, 645.458, NULL),
  (23864, 124, 'I don’t have to think about', 645.458, 648.210, NULL),
  (23865, 124, 'Progeria as an entity.', 648.210, 651.802, NULL),
  (23866, 124, 'Okay, pretty good, huh?', 655.905, 657.507, NULL),
  (23867, 124, '(Applause)', 657.507, 661.596, NULL),
  (23868, 124, 'Thank you.', 661.596, 662.671, NULL),
  (23869, 124, 'So, as you can see I’ve been
thinking this way for many years.', 662.671, 665.990, NULL),
  (23870, 124, 'But I’d never really had to apply
all of these aspects of my philosophy', 665.990, 670.435, NULL),
  (23871, 124, 'to the test at one time, 
until last January.', 670.435, 674.176, NULL),
  (23872, 124, 'I was pretty sick, I had a chest cold,
and I was in the hospital for a few days,', 674.176, 679.010, NULL),
  (23873, 124, 'and I was secluded from 
all of the aspects of my life that I felt', 679.010, 683.600, NULL),
  (23874, 124, 'made me, me,', 683.600, 685.124, NULL),
  (23875, 124, 'that kind of gave me my identity.', 685.124, 687.952, NULL),
  (23876, 124, 'But knowing
that I was going to get better,', 687.952, 691.029, NULL),
  (23877, 124, 'and looking forward to a time
that I would feel good again,', 691.029, 694.009, NULL),
  (23878, 124, 'helped me to keep moving forward.', 694.009, 696.659, NULL),
  (23879, 124, 'And sometimes I had to be brave,', 696.659, 699.211, NULL),
  (23880, 124, 'and it wasn’t always easy.', 699.211, 701.003, NULL),
  (23881, 124, 'Sometimes I faltered,', 701.003, 702.617, NULL),
  (23882, 124, 'I had bad days,', 702.617, 704.363, NULL),
  (23883, 124, 'but I realized that being brave
isn’t supposed to be easy.', 704.363, 707.857, NULL),
  (23884, 124, 'And for me, I feel it’s the key way
to keep moving forward.', 707.857, 711.957, NULL),
  (23885, 124, 'So, all in all,', 711.957, 714.181, NULL),
  (23886, 124, 'I don’t waste energy
feeling bad for myself.', 714.181, 717.725, NULL),
  (23887, 124, 'I surround myself with people
that I want to be with,', 717.725, 721.040, NULL),
  (23888, 124, 'and I keep moving forward.', 721.040, 723.317, NULL),
  (23889, 124, 'So with this philosophy,
I hope that all of you,', 723.317, 726.689, NULL),
  (23890, 124, 'regardless of your obstacles,', 726.689, 728.766, NULL),
  (23891, 124, 'can have a very happy life as well.', 728.766, 731.613, NULL),
  (23892, 124, 'Oh, wait, hang on a second,', 731.613, 733.131, NULL),
  (23893, 124, 'one more piece of advice –-', 733.131, 735.619, NULL),
  (23894, 124, '(Laughter)', 735.619, 737.219, NULL),
  (23895, 124, 'Never miss a party if you can help it.', 737.219, 739.709, NULL),
  (23896, 124, 'My school’s homecoming dance
is tomorrow night,', 739.709, 742.085, NULL),
  (23897, 124, 'and I will be there.', 742.085, 744.169, NULL),
  (23898, 124, 'Thank you very much.', 744.169, 745.641, NULL),
  (23899, 124, '(Applause)', 745.641, 751.295, NULL),
  (23900, 125, 'Transcriber: Gustavo Rocha
Reviewer: Marssi Draw', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (23901, 125, 'Hi everyone.', 9.003, 11.065, NULL),
  (23902, 125, 'Two year ago, my life changed forever.', 11.825, 16.625, NULL),
  (23903, 125, 'My wife Kelsey and I', 16.625, 19.261, NULL),
  (23904, 125, 'welcomed our daughter Lela
into the world.', 19.261, 23.033, NULL),
  (23905, 125, 'Now, becoming a parent
is an amazing experience.', 23.033, 27.456, NULL),
  (23906, 125, 'Your whole world changes over night.', 27.456, 30.704, NULL),
  (23907, 125, 'And all of your priorities
change immediately.', 30.704, 33.285, NULL),
  (23908, 125, 'So fast that it makes it really difficult
to process sometimes.', 33.285, 39.294, NULL),
  (23909, 125, 'Now, you also have to learn
a tremendous amount about being a parent', 39.294, 43.547, NULL),
  (23910, 125, 'like, for example,
how to dress your child.', 43.547, 46.820, NULL),
  (23911, 125, '(Laughter)', 46.820, 47.954, NULL),
  (23912, 125, 'This was new to me.', 47.954, 50.091, NULL),
  (23913, 125, 'This is an actual outfit, 
I thought this was a good idea.', 50.091, 53.844, NULL),
  (23914, 125, 'And even Lela knows
that it''s not a good idea. (Laughter)', 53.844, 59.558, NULL),
  (23915, 125, 'So there is so much to learn and
so much craziness all at once.', 59.558, 64.409, NULL),
  (23916, 125, 'And to add to the craziness, 
Kelsey and I both work from home,', 64.409, 68.533, NULL),
  (23917, 125, 'we''re entrepreneurs,
we run our own businesses.', 68.533, 71.223, NULL),
  (23918, 125, 'So, Kelsey develops courses
online for yoga teachers.', 71.223, 76.992, NULL),
  (23919, 125, 'I''m an author.', 76.992, 78.333, NULL),
  (23920, 125, 'And so, I''m working from home,
Kelsey''s working from home.', 78.333, 80.782, NULL),
  (23921, 125, 'We have an infant
and we''re trying to make sure', 80.782, 83.901, NULL),
  (23922, 125, 'that everything gets done
that needs done.', 83.901, 86.725, NULL),
  (23923, 125, 'And life is really, really busy.', 86.725, 91.107, NULL),
  (23924, 125, 'And a couple of weeks
into this amazing experience,', 92.357, 96.718, NULL),
  (23925, 125, 'when the sleep deprivation
really kicked in,', 96.718, 100.247, NULL),
  (23926, 125, 'like around week eight,', 100.247, 102.299, NULL),
  (23927, 125, 'I had this thought,
and it was the same thought', 102.299, 105.732, NULL),
  (23928, 125, 'that parents across the ages,
internationally,', 105.732, 109.773, NULL),
  (23929, 125, 'everybody has had this thought,
which is:', 109.773, 112.467, NULL),
  (23930, 125, 'I am never going to have
free time ever again.', 112.467, 118.054, NULL),
  (23931, 125, '(Laughter)', 118.054, 119.183, NULL),
  (23932, 125, 'Somebody said it''s true.', 119.183, 122.403, NULL),
  (23933, 125, 'It''s not exactly true,', 122.403, 125.214, NULL),
  (23934, 125, 'but it feels really, really true
in that moment.', 125.214, 129.866, NULL),
  (23935, 125, 'And this was really
disconcerning to me,', 129.866, 132.075, NULL),
  (23936, 125, 'because one of the things that I enjoy', 132.075, 135.484, NULL),
  (23937, 125, 'more than anything else
is learning new things.', 135.484, 139.428, NULL),
  (23938, 125, 'Getting curious about something
and diving in', 139.428, 142.261, NULL),
  (23939, 125, 'and fiddling around and 
learning through trial and error.', 142.261, 145.164, NULL),
  (23940, 125, 'And eventually becoming pretty good
at something.', 145.164, 148.440, NULL),
  (23941, 125, 'And without this free time,', 148.440, 152.336, NULL),
  (23942, 125, 'I didn''t know how I was ever 
going to do that ever again.', 152.336, 156.405, NULL),
  (23943, 125, 'And so, I''m a big geek,', 156.405, 158.877, NULL),
  (23944, 125, 'I want to keep learning things,
I want to keep growing.', 158.877, 162.070, NULL),
  (23945, 125, 'And so what I''ve decided to do was,', 162.070, 165.087, NULL),
  (23946, 125, 'go to the library,
and go to the bookstore,', 165.087, 167.784, NULL),
  (23947, 125, 'and look at what research says about', 167.784, 169.922, NULL),
  (23948, 125, 'how we learn and how we learn quickly.', 169.922, 173.523, NULL),
  (23949, 125, 'And I read a bunch of books,
I read a bunch of websites.', 173.523, 176.834, NULL),
  (23950, 125, 'And tried to answer this question,', 176.834, 179.091, NULL),
  (23951, 125, 'how long does it take
to acquire a new skill?', 179.091, 183.040, NULL),
  (23952, 125, 'You know what I found?', 183.040, 185.117, NULL),
  (23953, 125, '10,000 hours!', 185.117, 189.438, NULL),
  (23954, 125, 'Anybody ever heard this?', 189.438, 191.200, NULL),
  (23955, 125, 'It takes 10,000 hours.
If you want to learn something new,', 191.200, 194.134, NULL),
  (23956, 125, 'if you want to be good at it,', 194.134, 195.574, NULL),
  (23957, 125, 'it''s going to take 10,000 hours
to get there.', 195.584, 197.934, NULL),
  (23958, 125, 'And I read this in book after book,
in website after website.', 197.934, 201.455, NULL),
  (23959, 125, 'And my mental experience
of reading all of this stuff was like:', 201.455, 208.421, NULL),
  (23960, 125, 'No!!', 208.421, 210.799, NULL),
  (23961, 125, 'I don''t have time!
I don''t have 10,000 hours.', 210.799, 214.539, NULL),
  (23962, 125, 'I am never going to be able
to learn anything new.', 214.539, 219.088, NULL),
  (23963, 125, 'Ever again.
(Laughter)', 219.088, 222.421, NULL),
  (23964, 125, 'But that''s not true.', 222.421, 223.479, NULL),
  (23965, 125, 'So, 10,000 hours, just to give you
a rough order of magnitude,', 223.479, 226.559, NULL),
  (23966, 125, '10,000 hours is a full-time job
for five years.', 226.559, 232.422, NULL),
  (23967, 125, 'That''s a long time.', 232.422, 234.008, NULL),
  (23968, 125, 'And we''ve all had the experience
of learning something new,', 234.008, 236.364, NULL),
  (23969, 125, 'and it didn''t take us anywhere
close to that amount of time, right?', 236.364, 240.439, NULL),
  (23970, 125, 'So, what''s up? There''s something
kinda funky going on here.', 240.439, 243.505, NULL),
  (23971, 125, 'What the research says and what we expect,
and have experiences,', 243.505, 247.078, NULL),
  (23972, 125, 'they don''t match up.', 247.078, 249.416, NULL),
  (23973, 125, 'And what I found, here''s the wrinkle:', 249.416, 252.993, NULL),
  (23974, 125, 'The 10,000 hour rule came out of studies
of expert-level performance.', 252.993, 259.722, NULL),
  (23975, 125, 'There''s a professor
at Florida State University,', 259.722, 262.228, NULL),
  (23976, 125, 'his name is K. Anders Ericsson.', 262.228, 264.226, NULL),
  (23977, 125, 'He is the originator
of the 10,00 hour rule.', 264.226, 266.725, NULL),
  (23978, 125, 'And where that came from is,
he studied professional athletes,', 266.725, 271.261, NULL),
  (23979, 125, 'world class musicians,
chess grand masters.', 271.261, 275.763, NULL),
  (23980, 125, 'All of this ultra competitive folks
in ultra-high performing fields.', 275.763, 280.775, NULL),
  (23981, 125, 'And he tried to figure out
how long does it take', 280.775, 283.751, NULL),
  (23982, 125, 'to get to the top
of those kinds of fields.', 283.751, 286.811, NULL),
  (23983, 125, 'And what he found is,
the more deliberate practice,', 286.811, 289.668, NULL),
  (23984, 125, 'the more time
that those individuals spend', 289.668, 292.194, NULL),
  (23985, 125, 'practicing the elements
of whatever it is that they do,', 292.194, 295.304, NULL),
  (23986, 125, 'the more time you spend,
the better you get.', 295.304, 297.246, NULL),
  (23987, 125, 'And the folks at the tippy top
of their fields', 297.246, 300.165, NULL),
  (23988, 125, 'put in around 10,000 hours of practice.', 300.165, 305.101, NULL),
  (23989, 125, 'Now, we were talking about the game
of telephone a little bit earlier.', 305.101, 309.442, NULL),
  (23990, 125, 'Here''s what happened:', 309.442, 311.236, NULL),
  (23991, 125, 'an author by the name
of Malcolm Gladwell', 311.236, 313.458, NULL),
  (23992, 125, 'wrote a book in 2007 called
"Outliers: The Story of Success",', 313.458, 317.901, NULL),
  (23993, 125, 'and the central piece of that book
was the 10,000 hour rule.', 317.901, 321.592, NULL),
  (23994, 125, 'Practice a lot, practice well,
and you will do extremely well,', 321.592, 325.642, NULL),
  (23995, 125, 'you will reach the top of your field.', 325.642, 327.367, NULL),
  (23996, 125, 'So, the message,', 327.367, 329.472, NULL),
  (23997, 125, 'what Dr. Ericsson was actually saying is,', 329.472, 332.455, NULL),
  (23998, 125, 'it takes 10,000 hours to get
at the top of an ultra competitive field', 332.455, 337.425, NULL),
  (23999, 125, 'in a very narrow subject,
that''s what that means.', 337.425, 341.857, NULL),
  (24000, 125, 'But here''s what happened:
ever since Outliers came out,', 341.857, 345.294, NULL),
  (24001, 125, 'immediately came out,
reached the top of best seller lists,', 345.294, 347.449, NULL),
  (24002, 125, 'stayed there for three solid months.', 347.449, 350.056, NULL),
  (24003, 125, 'All of a sudden the 10,000 hour rule
was everywhere.', 350.056, 354.171, NULL),
  (24004, 125, 'And a society-wide game of telephone
started to be played.', 354.171, 360.022, NULL),
  (24005, 125, 'So this message, it takes 10,000 hours
to reach the top of an ultra competitive field,', 360.022, 364.955, NULL),
  (24006, 125, 'became, it takes 10,000 hours
to become an expert at something,', 364.955, 369.927, NULL),
  (24007, 125, 'which became,', 369.927, 371.366, NULL),
  (24008, 125, 'it takes 10,000 hours to become
good at something,', 371.366, 375.667, NULL),
  (24009, 125, 'which became,', 375.667, 377.192, NULL),
  (24010, 125, 'it takes 10,000 hours
to learn something.', 377.192, 381.455, NULL),
  (24011, 125, 'But that last statement,
it takes 10,000 hours to learn something,', 381.455, 385.337, NULL),
  (24012, 125, 'is not true.
It''s not true.', 385.337, 388.600, NULL),
  (24013, 125, 'So, what the research actually says --', 388.600, 393.346, NULL),
  (24014, 125, 'I spent a lot of time here
at the CSU library', 393.346, 396.217, NULL),
  (24015, 125, 'in the cognitive psychology stacks
''cause I''m a geek.', 396.217, 399.523, NULL),
  (24016, 125, 'And when you actually look
at the studies of skill acquisition,', 399.523, 404.216, NULL),
  (24017, 125, 'you see over and over
a graph like this.', 404.216, 408.039, NULL),
  (24018, 125, 'Now, researchers,
whether they''re studying a motor skill,', 408.039, 411.694, NULL),
  (24019, 125, 'something you do physically
or a mental skill,', 411.694, 414.328, NULL),
  (24020, 125, 'they like to study things
that they can time.', 414.328, 417.174, NULL),
  (24021, 125, '''Cause you can quantify that, right?', 417.174, 419.185, NULL),
  (24022, 125, 'So, they''ll give research participants
a little task,', 419.185, 422.452, NULL),
  (24023, 125, 'something that requires
physical arrangement,', 422.452, 424.156, NULL),
  (24024, 125, 'or something that requires
learning a little mental trick,', 424.156, 428.925, NULL),
  (24025, 125, 'and they''ll time how long a participant
takes to complete the skill.', 428.925, 433.357, NULL),
  (24026, 125, 'And here''s what this graph says,
when you start --', 433.357, 436.095, NULL),
  (24027, 125, 'so when researchers gave participants
a task, it took them a really long time,', 436.095, 440.398, NULL),
  (24028, 125, '''cause it was new
and they were horrible.', 440.398, 443.053, NULL),
  (24029, 125, 'With a little bit of practice,
they get better and better and better.', 443.053, 446.651, NULL),
  (24030, 125, 'And that early part of practice
is really, really efficient.', 446.651, 450.632, NULL),
  (24031, 125, 'People get good at things
with just a little bit of practice.', 450.632, 456.021, NULL),
  (24032, 125, 'Now, what''s interesting to note is that,', 456.021, 459.663, NULL),
  (24033, 125, 'for skills that we want to learn
for ourselves,', 459.663, 462.869, NULL),
  (24034, 125, 'we don''t care so much about time,
right?', 462.869, 465.736, NULL),
  (24035, 125, 'We just care about how good we are,
whatever good happens to mean.', 465.736, 469.283, NULL),
  (24036, 125, 'So if we relabel performance time
to how good you are,', 469.283, 474.943, NULL),
  (24037, 125, 'the graph flips, and you get
his famous and widely known,', 474.943, 479.346, NULL),
  (24038, 125, 'this is the learning curve.', 479.346, 481.274, NULL),
  (24039, 125, 'And the story of the learning curve
is when you start,', 481.274, 483.852, NULL),
  (24040, 125, 'you''re grossly incompetent
and you know it, right?', 483.852, 486.567, NULL),
  (24041, 125, '(Laughter)', 486.567, 488.635, NULL),
  (24042, 125, 'With a little bit of practice,
you get really good, really quick.', 488.635, 491.997, NULL),
  (24043, 125, 'So that early level of improvement
is really fast.', 491.997, 495.715, NULL),
  (24044, 125, 'And then at a certain point
you reach a plateau,', 495.715, 498.630, NULL),
  (24045, 125, 'and the subsequent games
become much harder to get,', 498.630, 501.960, NULL),
  (24046, 125, 'they take more time to get.', 501.960, 504.659, NULL),
  (24047, 125, 'Now, my question is,
I want that, right?', 504.659, 508.620, NULL),
  (24048, 125, 'How long does it take
from starting something', 508.620, 511.605, NULL),
  (24049, 125, 'and being grossly incompetent
and knowing it', 511.605, 515.265, NULL),
  (24050, 125, 'to being reasonably good?', 515.265, 517.575, NULL),
  (24051, 125, 'In hopefully, as short a period of time
as possible.', 517.575, 522.329, NULL),
  (24052, 125, 'So, how long does that take?', 522.329, 524.539, NULL),
  (24053, 125, 'Here''s what my research says: 20 hours.', 524.539, 529.518, NULL),
  (24054, 125, 'That''s it.
You can go from knowing nothing', 529.518, 533.163, NULL),
  (24055, 125, 'about any skill that you can think of.', 533.163, 535.739, NULL),
  (24056, 125, 'Want to learn a language?
Want to learn how to draw?', 535.739, 539.175, NULL),
  (24057, 125, 'Want to learn how to juggle
flaming chainsaws?', 539.175, 542.294, NULL),
  (24058, 125, '(Laughter)', 542.294, 543.320, NULL),
  (24059, 125, 'If you put 20 hours of focused
deliberate practice into that thing,', 543.320, 548.532, NULL),
  (24060, 125, 'you will be astounded.', 548.532, 550.964, NULL),
  (24061, 125, 'Astounded at how good you are.', 550.964, 554.135, NULL),
  (24062, 125, '20 hours is doable,', 554.135, 555.645, NULL),
  (24063, 125, 'that''s about 45 minutes a day
for about a month.', 555.645, 559.956, NULL),
  (24064, 125, 'Even skipping a couple days,
here and there.', 559.956, 562.066, NULL),
  (24065, 125, '20 hours isn''t that hard to accumulate.', 562.066, 565.221, NULL),
  (24066, 125, 'Now, there''s a method to doing this.', 565.221, 568.100, NULL),
  (24067, 125, 'Because it''s not like you can just start
fiddling around for about 20 hours', 568.100, 571.097, NULL),
  (24068, 125, 'and expect these massive improvements.', 571.097, 573.044, NULL),
  (24069, 125, 'There''s a way to practice intelligently.', 573.044, 575.713, NULL),
  (24070, 125, 'There''s a way to practice efficiently,', 575.713, 577.997, NULL),
  (24071, 125, 'that will make sure that you invest
those 20 hours', 577.997, 581.051, NULL),
  (24072, 125, 'in the most effective way
that you possibly can.', 581.051, 583.592, NULL),
  (24073, 125, 'And here''s the method,
it applies to anything:', 583.592, 587.518, NULL),
  (24074, 125, 'The first is to deconstruct the skill.', 587.518, 591.363, NULL),
  (24075, 125, 'Decide exactly what you want
to be able to do when you''re done,', 591.363, 596.262, NULL),
  (24076, 125, 'and then look into the skill
and break it down into smaller pieces.', 596.262, 602.072, NULL),
  (24077, 125, 'Most of the things
that we think of as skills', 602.072, 606.042, NULL),
  (24078, 125, 'are actually big bundles of skills
that require all sorts of different things.', 606.042, 610.639, NULL),
  (24079, 125, 'The more you can break apart the skill,', 610.639, 614.211, NULL),
  (24080, 125, 'the more you''re able to decide,', 614.211, 616.583, NULL),
  (24081, 125, 'what are the parts of this skill
that would actually help me', 616.583, 618.974, NULL),
  (24082, 125, 'get to what I want?', 618.974, 621.365, NULL),
  (24083, 125, 'And then you can practice those first.', 621.365, 623.758, NULL),
  (24084, 125, 'And if you practice
the most important things first,', 623.758, 625.960, NULL),
  (24085, 125, 'you''ll be able to improve
your performance', 625.960, 628.731, NULL),
  (24086, 125, 'in the least amount of time possible.', 628.731, 631.502, NULL),
  (24087, 125, 'The second is, learn enough
to self correct.', 631.502, 634.273, NULL),
  (24088, 125, 'So, get three to five resources
about what it is you''re trying to learn.', 634.273, 638.467, NULL),
  (24089, 125, 'Could be book, could be DVDs,
could be courses, could be anything.', 638.467, 643.719, NULL),
  (24090, 125, 'But don''t use those as a way
to procrastinate on practice.', 643.719, 648.950, NULL),
  (24091, 125, 'I know I do this, right?', 648.950, 650.585, NULL),
  (24092, 125, 'Get like 20 books about the topic,
like,', 650.585, 652.661, NULL),
  (24093, 125, '"I''m going to start learning
how to program a computer', 652.661, 655.138, NULL),
  (24094, 125, 'when I complete these 20 books".', 655.138, 657.615, NULL),
  (24095, 125, 'No. That''s procrastination.', 657.615, 660.094, NULL),
  (24096, 125, 'What you want to do
is learn just enough', 660.094, 664.141, NULL),
  (24097, 125, 'that you can actually practice', 664.141, 665.850, NULL),
  (24098, 125, 'and self correct or self edit
as you practice.', 665.850, 670.914, NULL),
  (24099, 125, 'So the learning becomes
a way of getting better', 670.914, 673.819, NULL),
  (24100, 125, 'at noticing
when you''re making a mistake', 673.819, 676.724, NULL),
  (24101, 125, 'and then doing something
a little different.', 676.724, 679.630, NULL),
  (24102, 125, 'The third is to remove barriers
to practice.', 679.630, 684.106, NULL),
  (24103, 125, 'Distractions, television, internet.', 684.106, 686.550, NULL),
  (24104, 125, 'All of these things
that get in the way', 686.550, 689.929, NULL),
  (24105, 125, 'of you actually sitting down
and doing the work.', 689.929, 693.308, NULL),
  (24106, 125, 'And the more you''re able to use
just a little bit of willpower', 693.308, 696.689, NULL),
  (24107, 125, 'to remove the distractions that
are keeping you from practicing,', 696.689, 699.887, NULL),
  (24108, 125, 'the more likely you are to actually
sit down and practice, right?', 699.887, 706.270, NULL),
  (24109, 125, 'And the fourth is to practice
for at least 20 hours.', 706.270, 711.473, NULL),
  (24110, 125, 'Now, most skills have what I call
a frustration barrier.', 711.473, 714.770, NULL),
  (24111, 125, 'You know, the grossly-incompetent-
and-knowing-it part?', 714.770, 718.078, NULL),
  (24112, 125, 'That''s really, really frustrating.
We don''t like to feel stupid.', 718.078, 722.374, NULL),
  (24113, 125, 'And feeling stupid is a barrier to us 
actually sitting down and doing the work.', 722.374, 727.314, NULL),
  (24114, 125, 'So, by pre-committing to practicing
whatever it is that you want to do', 727.314, 731.762, NULL),
  (24115, 125, 'for at least 20 hours,', 731.762, 734.378, NULL),
  (24116, 125, 'you will be able to overcome
that initial frustration barrier', 734.378, 738.918, NULL),
  (24117, 125, 'and stick with the practice long enough
to actually reap the rewards.', 738.918, 743.029, NULL),
  (24118, 125, 'That''s it! It''s not rocket science.', 743.029, 745.368, NULL),
  (24119, 125, 'Four very simple steps that
you can use to learn anything.', 745.368, 750.479, NULL),
  (24120, 125, 'Now, this is easy to talk
