  (24385, 126, 'The first example is:', 526.792, 528.782, NULL),
  (24386, 126, 'I''ve worked a lot with children
and students in schools.', 528.782, 531.752, NULL),
  (24387, 126, 'Actually the little ones,
they just draw fine,', 531.752, 534.002, NULL),
  (24388, 126, 'but when they get to about 15 or 16,
most of them think they can''t draw.', 534.002, 537.582, NULL),
  (24389, 126, 'But I worked with them.', 537.582, 538.782, NULL),
  (24390, 126, 'I worked this week in a school', 538.782, 540.912, NULL),
  (24391, 126, 'where I was coaching them
on using pictures for memory.', 540.912, 544.242, NULL),
  (24392, 126, 'A girl was trying to remember
what red blood cells do,', 544.242, 548.262, NULL),
  (24393, 126, 'and she drew this little picture', 548.262, 549.862, NULL),
  (24394, 126, 'of a red blood cell
carrying a handbag with O2 on it', 549.862, 553.242, NULL),
  (24395, 126, 'to remind her that the red blood cells
carry oxygen to all parts of the body.', 553.242, 557.802, NULL),
  (24396, 126, 'That was a great one.', 557.802, 559.252, NULL),
  (24397, 126, 'The other people I worked with
are many adults in all walks of life,', 559.252, 562.552, NULL),
  (24398, 126, 'and particularly in business,', 562.552, 564.782, NULL),
  (24399, 126, 'and they often will want
to make presentations memorable.', 564.782, 568.232, NULL),
  (24400, 126, 'So again, a quick cartoon or sketch
could be really good for that.', 568.232, 572.242, NULL),
  (24401, 126, 'And again, most people think
