  (24881, 128, 'Transcriber: Translate TED
Reviewer: Allam Zedan', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (24882, 128, 'The people in the back,
can you hear me clearly?', 10.159, 12.722, NULL),
  (24883, 128, 'OK, good.', 13.030, 14.124, NULL),
  (24884, 128, 'Have you ever held a question in mind', 15.571, 19.496, NULL),
  (24885, 128, 'for so long that it becomes
part of how you think?', 19.496, 24.391, NULL),
  (24886, 128, 'Maybe even part of who you are
as a person?', 25.237, 28.164, NULL),
  (24887, 128, 'Well I''ve had a question in my mind 
for many, many years', 28.795, 32.876, NULL),
  (24888, 128, 'and that is: 
How can you speed up learning?', 32.876, 37.224, NULL),
  (24889, 128, 'Now, this is an interesting question', 38.085, 40.648, NULL),
  (24890, 128, 'because if you speed up learning,', 40.648, 42.359, NULL),
  (24891, 128, 'you can spend less time at school.', 42.359, 44.000, NULL),
  (24892, 128, 'And if you learn really fast,', 44.970, 47.099, NULL),
  (24893, 128, 'you probably 
wouldn''t have to go to school at all.', 47.119, 49.878, NULL),
  (24894, 128, 'Now, when I was young, 
school was sort of OK but...', 50.818, 53.877, NULL),
  (24895, 128, 'I found quite often that school 
got in the way of learning', 54.983, 58.289, NULL),
  (24896, 128, 'so I had this question in mind: 
How do you learn faster?', 58.859, 61.785, NULL),
  (24897, 128, 'And this began when I was 
very, very young,', 62.523, 65.821, NULL),
  (24898, 128, 'when I was 11 years old,', 65.821, 67.497, NULL),
  (24899, 128, 'I wrote a letter to researchers in the 
Soviet Union, asking about hypnopaedia,', 67.497, 71.882, NULL),
  (24900, 128, 'this is sleep-learning,', 71.882, 73.922, NULL),
  (24901, 128, 'where you get a tape recorder, 
you put it beside your bed', 73.922, 76.892, NULL),
  (24902, 128, 'and it turns on 
in the middle of the night', 76.892, 79.006, NULL),
  (24903, 128, 'when you''re sleeping,', 79.006, 80.439, NULL),
  (24904, 128, 'and you''re supposed to be 
learning from this.', 80.439, 82.652, NULL),
  (24905, 128, 'A good idea, 
unfortunately it doesn''t work.', 82.688, 85.468, NULL),
  (24906, 128, 'But, hypnopaedia did open the doors 
to research in other areas', 85.468, 89.783, NULL),
  (24907, 128, 'and we''ve had 
incredible discoveries about ', 89.783, 92.083, NULL),
  (24908, 128, 'learning that began 
with that first question.', 92.083, 94.933, NULL),
  (24909, 128, 'I went on from there to become 
passionate about psychology', 96.123, 99.293, NULL),
  (24910, 128, 'and I have been involved in psychology
in many different ways', 99.293, 103.149, NULL),
  (24911, 128, 'for the rest of my life 
up until this point.', 103.149, 105.968, NULL),
  (24912, 128, 'In 1981, I took myself to China', 105.968, 109.615, NULL),
  (24913, 128, 'and I decided that I was going to be 
native level in Chinese inside two years.', 109.985, 116.044, NULL),
  (24914, 128, 'Now, you need to understand that 
in 1981, everybody thought', 116.674, 121.530, NULL),
  (24915, 128, 'Chinese was really, really difficult', 121.530, 124.012, NULL),
  (24916, 128, 'and that a Westerner 
could study for 10 years or more', 124.012, 126.494, NULL),
  (24917, 128, 'and never really get very good at it.', 126.494, 128.977, NULL),
  (24918, 128, 'And I also went in with a different idea', 128.977, 131.082, NULL),
  (24919, 128, 'which was: taking all of the conclusions', 131.082, 133.633, NULL),
  (24920, 128, 'from psychological research 
up to that point', 133.633, 136.184, NULL),
  (24921, 128, 'and applying them 
to the learning process.', 136.184, 138.735, NULL),
  (24922, 128, 'What was really cool was that in six 
