  (24986, 128, 'struggling extremely, extremely... 
a great deal', 363.506, 366.758, NULL),
  (24987, 128, 'and finally people were saying: 
"You''re completely useless,"', 366.758, 369.336, NULL),
  (24988, 128, '"you''re not talented," "give up," 
"you''re a waste of time"', 369.336, 373.506, NULL),
  (24989, 128, 'and she was very, very depressed.', 373.506, 375.074, NULL),
  (24990, 128, 'And then she came across 
these five principles,', 375.074, 377.376, NULL),
  (24991, 128, 'she moved to Brazil and she applied them', 377.376, 379.914, NULL),
  (24992, 128, 'and in six months 
she was fluent in Portuguese,', 379.914, 382.595, NULL),
  (24993, 128, 'so talent doesn''t matter.', 382.605, 384.240, NULL),
  (24994, 128, 'People also think that immersion in a new 
country is the way to learn a language.', 384.508, 388.722, NULL),
  (24995, 128, 'But look around Hong Kong, 
look at all the westerners', 388.722, 391.308, NULL),
  (24996, 128, 'who''ve been here for 10 years, 
who don''t speak a word of Chinese.', 391.308, 394.635, NULL),
  (24997, 128, 'Look at all the Chinese living in 
America, Britain, Australia, Canada', 395.587, 399.084, NULL),
  (24998, 128, 'have been there 10, 20 years 
and they don''t speak any English.', 399.084, 402.965, NULL),
  (24999, 128, 'Immersion per se does not work.', 403.840, 405.834, NULL),
  (25000, 128, 'Why? Because a drowning man 
cannot learn to swim.', 405.834, 408.672, NULL),
  (25001, 128, 'When you don''t speak a language, 
you''re like a baby.', 409.873, 412.474, NULL),
  (25002, 128, 'And if you drop yourself into a context', 412.474, 414.459, NULL),
  (25003, 128, 'which is all adults talking about stuff 
over your head, you won''t learn.', 414.459, 418.139, NULL),
  (25004, 128, 'So, what are the five principles 
that you need to pay attention to?', 419.032, 422.367, NULL),
  (25005, 128, 'First: the four words,', 422.367, 424.740, NULL),
  (25006, 128, 'attention, meaning, relevance and memory,', 424.740, 426.750, NULL),
  (25007, 128, 'and these interconnect in very, 
very important ways.', 426.750, 429.676, NULL),
  (25008, 128, 'Especially when you''re talking 
about learning.', 430.214, 432.464, NULL),
  (25009, 128, 'Come with me on a journey 
through a forest.', 432.474, 434.933, NULL),
  (25010, 128, 'You go on a walk through a forest', 434.933, 437.306, NULL),
  (25011, 128, 'and you see something like this... 
Little marks on a tree,', 437.306, 440.883, NULL),
  (25012, 128, 'maybe you pay attention, maybe you don''t.', 440.883, 442.957, NULL),
  (25013, 128, 'You go another 50 metres 
and you see this...', 443.957, 446.267, NULL),
  (25014, 128, 'You should be paying attention.', 446.267, 449.044, NULL),
  (25015, 128, 'Another 50 metres, if you haven''t been 
paying attention, you see this...', 449.684, 453.210, NULL),
  (25016, 128, 'And at this point,
you''re paying attention.', 453.401, 456.575, NULL),
  (25017, 128, 'And you''ve just learned that this...
is important,', 457.207, 460.211, NULL),
  (25018, 128, 'it''s relevant 
because it means this,', 460.211, 462.837, NULL),
  (25019, 128, 'and anything that is related, 
any information related to your survival', 462.837, 467.491, NULL),
  (25020, 128, 'is stuff that you''re going to pay
attention to', 468.037, 470.272, NULL),
  (25021, 128, 'and therefore you''re going
to remember it.', 470.272, 472.279, NULL),
  (25022, 128, 'If it''s related to your personal goals,', 472.279, 474.228, NULL),
  (25023, 128, 'then you''re going to pay attention to it.', 474.228, 476.270, NULL),
  (25024, 128, 'If it''s relevant, 
you''re going to remember it.', 476.270, 478.555, NULL),
  (25025, 128, 'So, the first rule, 
first principle for learning a language', 478.930, 481.746, NULL),
  (25026, 128, 'is focus on language content 
that is relevant to you.', 481.756, 484.309, NULL),
  (25027, 128, 'Which brings us to tools.', 484.309, 486.066, NULL),
  (25028, 128, 'We master tools by using tools 
and we learn tools the fastest', 487.220, 491.299, NULL),
  (25029, 128, 'when they are relevant to us.', 491.299, 493.915, NULL),
  (25030, 128, 'So let me share a story.', 494.484, 495.757, NULL),
  (25031, 128, 'A keyboard is a tool.', 495.757, 497.377, NULL),
  (25032, 128, 'Typing Chinese a certain way, 
there are methods for this. That''s a tool.', 498.192, 501.774, NULL),
  (25033, 128, 'I had a colleague many years ago', 501.774, 504.162, NULL),
  (25034, 128, 'who went to night school; 
Tuesday night, Thursday night,', 504.988, 507.651, NULL),
  (25035, 128, 'two hours each time, practicing at home,', 507.651, 509.975, NULL),
  (25036, 128, 'she spent nine months, 
and she did not learn to type Chinese.', 509.975, 513.659, NULL),
  (25037, 128, 'And one night we had a crisis.', 514.520, 516.398, NULL),
  (25038, 128, 'We had 48 hours to deliver 
a training manual in Chinese.', 516.587, 520.230, NULL),
  (25039, 128, 'And she got the job, 
and I can guarantee you', 520.636, 522.731, NULL),
  (25040, 128, 'in 48 hours, she learned to type Chinese', 522.731, 524.737, NULL),
  (25041, 128, 'because it was relevant,
it was meaningful, it was important,', 524.737, 527.643, NULL),
  (25042, 128, 'she was using a tool to create value.', 527.643, 530.146, NULL),
  (25043, 128, 'So the second principle for learning 
a language is to use your language', 530.156, 533.547, NULL),
  (25044, 128, 'as a tool to communicate 
right from day one.', 533.547, 536.811, NULL),
  (25045, 128, 'As a kid does.', 537.688, 539.051, NULL),
  (25046, 128, 'When I first arrived in China, 
I didn''t speak a word of Chinese,', 539.889, 542.964, NULL),
  (25047, 128, 'and on my second week, 
I got to take a train ride overnight.', 543.919, 547.435, NULL),
  (25048, 128, 'I spent eight hours sitting 
in the dining car', 547.948, 550.141, NULL),
  (25049, 128, 'talking to one of the guards on the train,', 550.141, 552.144, NULL),
  (25050, 128, 'he took an interest in me for some reason,', 552.144, 554.219, NULL),
  (25051, 128, 'and we just chatted all night in Chinese', 554.219, 557.063, NULL),
  (25052, 128, 'and he was drawing pictures and 
making movements with his hands', 557.063, 560.079, NULL),
  (25053, 128, 'and facial expressions 
and piece by piece by piece', 560.079, 562.786, NULL),
  (25054, 128, 'I understood more and more.', 562.786, 564.534, NULL),
  (25055, 128, 'But what was really cool, 
was two weeks later,', 565.409, 567.684, NULL),
  (25056, 128, 'when people were talking Chinese 
around me,', 568.237, 570.643, NULL),
  (25057, 128, 'I was understanding some of this', 570.643, 572.245, NULL),
  (25058, 128, 'and I hadn''t even made any effort 
to learn that.', 572.245, 574.804, NULL),
  (25059, 128, 'What had happened, 
I''d absorbed it that night on the train,', 575.366, 578.183, NULL),
  (25060, 128, 'which brings us to the third principle.', 578.183, 580.357, NULL),
  (25061, 128, 'When you first understand the message,', 580.397, 582.950, NULL),
  (25062, 128, 'then you will acquire 
the language unconsciously.', 583.584, 587.509, NULL),
  (25063, 128, 'And this is really, 
really well documented now,', 588.509, 591.115, NULL),
  (25064, 128, 'it''s something called 
comprehensible input.', 591.115, 593.166, NULL),
  (25065, 128, 'There''s 20 or 30 years 
of research on this,', 593.166, 595.234, NULL),
  (25066, 128, 'Stephen Krashen, a leader in the field,', 595.234, 597.164, NULL),
  (25067, 128, 'has published all sorts of 
these different studies', 597.164, 599.844, NULL),
  (25068, 128, 'and this is just from one of them.', 599.844, 601.661, NULL),
  (25069, 128, 'The purple bars show the scores 
on different tests for language.', 601.661, 606.797, NULL),
  (25070, 128, 'The purple people were people who had 
learned by grammar and formal study,', 609.611, 614.365, NULL),
  (25071, 128, 'the green ones are the ones 
who learned by comprehensible input.', 614.365, 617.424, NULL),
  (25072, 128, 'So, comprehension works. 
Comprehension is key', 617.497, 620.805, NULL),
  (25073, 128, 'and language learning is not about 
accumulating lots of knowledge.', 621.759, 627.147, NULL),
  (25074, 128, 'In many, many ways 
it''s about physiological training.', 628.947, 632.743, NULL),
  (25075, 128, 'A woman I know from Taiwan 
did great in English at school,', 634.159, 637.394, NULL),
  (25076, 128, 'she got A grades all the way through,', 637.394, 639.159, NULL),
  (25077, 128, 'went through college, A grades, 
went to the US', 639.159, 642.025, NULL),
  (25078, 128, 'and found she couldn''t understand 
what people were saying.', 642.025, 644.804, NULL),
  (25079, 128, 'And people started asking her: 
"Are you deaf?"', 645.514, 648.545, NULL),
  (25080, 128, 'And she was. English deaf.', 649.405, 651.831, NULL),
  (25081, 128, 'Because we have filters 
in our brain that filter in', 652.815, 656.106, NULL),
  (25082, 128, 'the sounds that we are familiar with', 656.106, 658.584, NULL),
  (25083, 128, 'and they filter out the sounds of 
languages that we''re not.', 658.584, 661.548, NULL),
  (25084, 128, 'And if you can''t hear it, 
you won''t understand it,', 662.633, 665.012, NULL),
  (25085, 128, 'if you can''t understand it, 
you''re not going to learn it.', 665.012, 667.720, NULL),
  (25086, 128, 'So you actually have to be 
able to hear these sounds.', 667.726, 670.260, NULL),
  (25087, 128, 'And there are ways to do that 
but it''s physiological training.', 670.260, 673.219, NULL),
  (25088, 128, 'Speaking takes muscle.', 673.219, 676.835, NULL),
  (25089, 128, 'You''ve got 43 muscles in your face,', 678.312, 680.752, NULL),
  (25090, 128, 'you have to coordinate those in a way', 681.215, 683.708, NULL),
  (25091, 128, 'that you make sounds that 
other people will understand.', 683.708, 686.501, NULL),
  (25092, 128, 'If you''ve ever done a new sport 
for a couple of days,', 687.455, 690.630, NULL),
  (25093, 128, 'and you know how your body feels? Hurts?', 690.630, 693.326, NULL),
  (25094, 128, 'If your face is hurting, 
you''re doing it right.', 693.802, 696.236, NULL),
  (25095, 128, 'And the final principle is state. 
Psycho-physiological state.', 698.651, 702.759, NULL),
  (25096, 128, 'If you''re sad, angry, worried, upset, 
you''re not going to learn. Period.', 703.204, 707.066, NULL),
  (25097, 128, 'If you''re happy, relaxed, 
in an Alpha brain state, curious,', 708.174, 711.824, NULL),
  (25098, 128, 'you''re going to learn really quickly,', 711.824, 713.863, NULL),
  (25099, 128, 'and very specifically you need
to be tolerant of ambiguity.', 713.863, 717.166, NULL),
  (25100, 128, 'If you''re one of those people 
who needs to understand 100 percent', 717.513, 720.602, NULL),
  (25101, 128, 'every word you''re hearing, 
you will go nuts,', 720.602, 723.462, NULL),
  (25102, 128, 'because you''ll be incredibly upset 
all the time, because you''re not perfect.', 723.462, 727.100, NULL),
  (25103, 128, 'If you''re comfortable with getting some, 
not getting some,', 727.810, 730.611, NULL),
  (25104, 128, 'just paying attention 
to what you do understand,', 731.030, 733.333, NULL),
  (25105, 128, 'you''re going to be fine, relaxed,
and you''ll be learning quickly.', 733.333, 736.852, NULL),
  (25106, 128, 'So based on those five principles, 
what are the seven actions that you take?', 736.852, 740.559, NULL),
  (25107, 128, 'Number one: Listen a lot.', 741.128, 743.001, NULL),
  (25108, 128, 'I call it brain soaking.', 743.647, 745.529, NULL),
  (25109, 128, 'You put yourself in a context', 746.198, 747.681, NULL),
  (25110, 128, 'where you''re hearing tons and tons 
and tons of a language', 747.691, 751.274, NULL),
  (25111, 128, 'and it doesn''t matter 
if you understand it or not.', 751.274, 753.779, NULL),
  (25112, 128, 'You''re listening to the rhythms, 
to patterns that repeat,', 753.785, 757.309, NULL),
  (25113, 128, 'you''re listening to things that stand out.', 757.309, 759.362, NULL),
  (25114, 128, '(Chinese) Pào nǎozi.', 759.362, 761.105, NULL),
  (25115, 128, '(English) So, just soak your brain in this.', 761.105, 763.599, NULL),
  (25116, 128, 'The second action is that 
you get the meaning first,', 763.611, 766.530, NULL),
  (25117, 128, 'even before you get the words.', 766.530, 768.469, NULL),
  (25118, 128, 'You go: "Well how do I do that? 
I don''t know the words!"', 768.469, 771.269, NULL),
  (25119, 128, 'Well, you understand what these 
different postures mean.', 771.269, 774.893, NULL),
  (25120, 128, 'Human communication is body language 
in many, many ways, so much body language.', 775.267, 780.192, NULL),
  (25121, 128, 'From body language you can 
understand a lot of communication,', 780.192, 783.401, NULL),
  (25122, 128, 'therefore, you''re understanding, you''re 
acquiring through comprehensible input.', 783.401, 787.693, NULL),
  (25123, 128, 'And you can also use patterns 
that you already know.', 787.693, 791.844, NULL),
  (25124, 128, 'If you''re a Chinese speaker of Mandarin 
and Cantonese and you go to Vietnam,', 791.844, 796.044, NULL),
  (25125, 128, 'you will understand 60 percent of what 
they say to you in daily conversation,', 796.643, 802.316, NULL),
  (25126, 128, 'because Vietnamese is about 30 percent 
Mandarin, 30 percent Cantonese.', 802.316, 806.810, NULL),
  (25127, 128, 'The third action: Start mixing.', 808.964, 811.313, NULL),
  (25128, 128, 'You probably have never thought of this', 811.463, 813.333, NULL),
  (25129, 128, 'but if you''ve got 10 verbs, 
10 nouns and 10 adjectives,', 813.333, 816.048, NULL),
  (25130, 128, 'you can say 1000 different things.', 816.068, 818.598, NULL),
  (25131, 128, 'Language is a creative process.', 819.996, 822.572, NULL),
  (25132, 128, 'What do babies do? OK, 
"me", "bath", "now".', 823.279, 827.205, NULL),
  (25133, 128, 'OK, that''s how they communicate.', 827.620, 829.245, NULL),
  (25134, 128, 'So start mixing, get creative, 
have fun with it,', 829.245, 831.851, NULL),
  (25135, 128, 'it doesn''t have to be perfect, 
just has to work.', 831.851, 834.264, NULL),
  (25136, 128, 'And when you''re doing this, 
you focus on the core.', 835.005, 838.212, NULL),
  (25137, 128, 'What does that mean?', 838.212, 839.827, NULL),
  (25138, 128, 'Well, any language is 
high frequency content.', 839.827, 842.665, NULL),
  (25139, 128, 'In English 1000 words covers 85 percent', 842.665, 846.370, NULL),
  (25140, 128, 'of anything you''re ever going 
to say in daily communication.', 846.370, 849.289, NULL),
  (25141, 128, '3000 words gives you 98 percent', 849.289, 852.015, NULL),
  (25142, 128, 'of anything you''re going to say
in daily conversation.', 852.015, 854.758, NULL),
  (25143, 128, 'You got 3000 words, 
you''re speaking the language.', 854.758, 857.489, NULL),
  (25144, 128, 'The rest is icing on the cake.', 857.489, 860.220, NULL),
  (25145, 128, 'And when you''re just beginning 
with a new language,', 860.220, 862.951, NULL),
  (25146, 128, 'start with your tool box. Week number one,', 862.951, 865.746, NULL),
  (25147, 128, 'in your new language you say things like:', 866.438, 868.709, NULL),
  (25148, 128, '"How do you say that?"
"I don''t understand,"', 868.709, 870.824, NULL),
  (25149, 128, '"repeat that please," 
"what does that mean?"', 870.824, 873.084, NULL),
  (25150, 128, 'all in your target language.', 873.084, 874.650, NULL),
  (25151, 128, 'You''re using it as a tool, 
making it useful to you,', 874.650, 877.966, NULL),
  (25152, 128, 'it''s relevant to learn other things 
about the language.', 877.966, 881.093, NULL),
  (25153, 128, 'By week two,
you should be saying things like:', 881.093, 883.954, NULL),
  (25154, 128, '"me," "this," "you," "that," 
"give," you know, "hot,"', 883.954, 887.654, NULL),
  (25155, 128, 'simple pronouns, 
simple nouns, simple verbs,', 887.654, 891.804, NULL),
  (25156, 128, 'simple adjectives, 
communicating like a baby.', 891.804, 894.324, NULL),
  (25157, 128, 'And by the third or fourth week, 
you''re getting into "glue words."', 894.324, 898.034, NULL),
  (25158, 128, '"Although," "but," "therefore," 
these are logical transformers', 899.126, 903.253, NULL),
  (25159, 128, 'that tie bits of a language together, 
allowing you to make more complex meaning.', 903.253, 908.108, NULL),
  (25160, 128, 'At that point you''re talking.', 908.108, 910.299, NULL),
  (25161, 128, 'And when you''re doing that, 
you should get yourself a language parent.', 910.960, 914.396, NULL),
  (25162, 128, 'If you look at how 
children and parents interact,', 915.703, 918.678, NULL),
  (25163, 128, 'you''ll understand what this means.', 918.678, 920.423, NULL),
  (25164, 128, 'When a child is speaking, it''ll be using 
simple words, simple combinations,', 921.113, 924.920, NULL),
  (25165, 128, 'sometimes quite strange, 
sometimes very strange pronunciation,', 924.990, 928.658, NULL),
  (25166, 128, 'other people from outside the family 
don''t understand it.', 928.658, 932.044, NULL),
  (25167, 128, 'But the parents do.', 932.828, 934.789, NULL),
  (25168, 128, 'And so the kid has a safe environment, 
gets confidence.', 934.789, 939.201, NULL),
  (25169, 128, 'The parents talk to the children 
with body language', 939.201, 942.039, NULL),
  (25170, 128, 'and with simple language they 
know the child understands.', 942.039, 945.120, NULL),
  (25171, 128, 'So you have a comprehensible input 
environment that''s safe,', 945.532, 948.383, NULL),
  (25172, 128, 'we know it works; otherwise none of you 
would speak your mother tongue.', 948.383, 952.303, NULL),
  (25173, 128, 'So you get yourself a language parent,', 952.842, 954.699, NULL),
  (25174, 128, 'who''s somebody interested in you 
as a person', 954.699, 956.836, NULL),
  (25175, 128, 'who will communicate with you 
essentially as an equal,', 956.836, 959.644, NULL),
  (25176, 128, 'but pay attention to help you 
understand the message.', 959.644, 961.961, NULL),
  (25177, 128, 'There are four rules of a language parent.', 964.278, 966.595, NULL),
  (25178, 128, 'Spouses are not very good at this, OK?', 966.595, 968.734, NULL),
  (25179, 128, 'But the four rules are,', 968.734, 969.894, NULL),
  (25180, 128, 'first of all, they will work hard 
to understand what you mean', 969.894, 972.826, NULL),
  (25181, 128, 'even when you''re way off beat.', 972.826, 975.278, NULL),
  (25182, 128, 'Secondly, they will never 
correct your mistakes.', 975.278, 977.971, NULL),
  (25183, 128, 'Thirdly, they will feed back 
their understanding of what you are saying', 978.710, 982.383, NULL),
  (25184, 128, 'so that you can respond appropriately 
and get that feedback', 982.383, 986.239, NULL),
  (25185, 128, 'and then they will use 
words that you know.', 986.239, 988.832, NULL),
  (25186, 128, 'The sixth thing you have to do, 
is copy the face.', 989.863, 993.188, NULL),
  (25187, 128, 'You got to get the muscles working right,', 993.188, 995.270, NULL),
  (25188, 128, 'so you can sound in a way that 
people will understand you.', 995.270, 998.597, NULL),
  (25189, 128, 'There''s a couple of things you do.', 999.260, 1000.885, NULL),
  (25190, 128, 'One is that you hear how it feels, 
and feel how it sounds', 1000.885, 1004.388, NULL),
  (25191, 128, 'which means you have a feedback loop 
operating in your face,', 1004.388, 1007.577, NULL),
  (25192, 128, 'but ideally if you can look at 
a native speaker', 1007.577, 1010.654, NULL),
  (25193, 128, 'and just observe 
how they use their face,', 1010.654, 1012.671, NULL),
  (25194, 128, 'let your unconscious mind 
absorb the rules,', 1012.671, 1015.536, NULL),
  (25195, 128, 'then you''re going to be 
able to pick it up.', 1015.536, 1017.931, NULL),
  (25196, 128, 'And if you can''t get a native speaker 
to look at, you can use stuff like this...', 1017.931, 1021.808, NULL),
  (25197, 128, '(Female voice) Sing, song, 
king, stung, hung.', 1022.329, 1031.969, NULL),
  (25198, 128, '(Chris Lonsdale) And the final idea here, 
the final action you need to take', 1032.475, 1036.064, NULL),
  (25199, 128, 'is something that I call "direct connect".', 1036.064, 1038.204, NULL),
  (25200, 128, 'What does this mean? Well most people 
learning a second language', 1038.204, 1041.369, NULL),
  (25201, 128, 'sort of take the mother tongue words 
and the target words and go over them', 1041.369, 1044.923, NULL),
  (25202, 128, 'again and again in their mind to try 
and remember them. Really inefficient.', 1044.923, 1048.710, NULL),
  (25203, 128, 'What you need to do is realise that', 1048.918, 1051.144, NULL),
  (25204, 128, 'everything you know is an image 
inside your mind, it''s feelings,', 1051.144, 1054.400, NULL),
  (25205, 128, 'if you talk about fire, 
you can smell the smoke,', 1054.400, 1056.736, NULL),
  (25206, 128, 'you can hear the crackling, 
you can see the flames,', 1056.736, 1059.362, NULL),
  (25207, 128, 'so what you do, is you go into 
that imagery and all of that memory', 1059.362, 1062.849, NULL),
  (25208, 128, 'and you come out with another pathway. 
So I call it "same box, different path".', 1062.849, 1067.289, NULL),
  (25209, 128, 'You come out of that pathway 
and you build it over time,', 1067.289, 1070.039, NULL),
  (25210, 128, 'you become more and more skilled 
at just connecting the new sounds', 1070.039, 1073.668, NULL),
  (25211, 128, 'to those images that you already have, 
into that internal representation.', 1073.668, 1077.983, NULL),
  (25212, 128, 'And over time you even become naturally 
good at that process,', 1078.798, 1081.740, NULL),
  (25213, 128, 'that becomes unconscious.', 1081.760, 1083.542, NULL),
  (25214, 128, 'So, there are five principles that you 
need to work with, seven actions,', 1083.582, 1088.374, NULL),
  (25215, 128, 'if you do any of them, 
you''re going to improve.', 1088.374, 1090.937, NULL),
  (25216, 128, 'And remember these are things 
under your control as the learner.', 1090.937, 1094.021, NULL),
  (25217, 128, 'Do them all and you''re going to be 
fluent in a second language in six months.', 1094.021, 1097.963, NULL),
  (25218, 128, 'Thank you.', 1097.963, 1099.352, NULL),
  (25219, 128, '(Applause)', 1099.352, 1100.132, NULL),
  (25220, 129, 'Transcriber: Judith Matz
