  (26491, 132, 'Just try a bunch of stuff.
See where it breaks.', 771.384, 774.406, NULL),
  (26492, 132, 'See what falls in my lap.', 774.406, 776.218, NULL),
  (26493, 132, 'When I find a hole like that
then I can start looking for an exploit.', 776.218, 781.282, NULL),
  (26494, 132, 'This is a little more what SSL looks
like to hackers, that''s really boring.', 781.282, 786.240, NULL),
  (26495, 132, 'This guy kills a million Africans a year.', 786.240, 790.747, NULL),
  (26496, 132, 'It''s Anopheles stephensi mosquito
carrying malaria.', 791.031, 794.791, NULL),
  (26497, 132, 'Is this the wrong talk?', 795.738, 797.788, NULL),
  (26498, 132, '(Laughter)', 797.788, 799.403, NULL),
  (26499, 132, 'This is a protocol diagram for malaria.', 799.403, 803.258, NULL),
  (26500, 132, 'So what we''re doing in our lab
is attacking this protocol', 803.892, 807.477, NULL),
  (26501, 132, 'at every point we can find.', 807.477, 809.681, NULL),
  (26502, 132, 'It has a very complex life cycle
that I won''t go into now,', 809.681, 812.758, NULL),
  (26503, 132, 'but it spends some time in humans,
some time in mosquitos', 812.758, 816.227, NULL),
  (26504, 132, 'and what I need are hackers.', 816.227, 819.467, NULL),
  (26505, 132, 'Because hackers have a mind
that''s optimized for discovery.', 819.467, 823.508, NULL),
  (26506, 132, 'They have a mind that''s optimized
for figuring out what''s possible.', 823.934, 827.407, NULL),
  (26507, 132, 'You know, I often illustrate this
by saying,', 827.407, 829.805, NULL),
  (26508, 132, 'If you get some random new
gadget and show it to your Mom,', 829.805, 834.676, NULL),
  (26509, 132, 'she might say, "Well, what does this do?"
And you''d say "Mom, it''s a phone."', 835.455, 839.245, NULL),
  (26510, 132, 'And instantly, she''d would know
exactly what it''s for.', 839.245, 842.566, NULL),
  (26511, 132, 'But with a hacker,
the question is different.', 842.566, 845.085, NULL),
  (26512, 132, 'The question is,
"What can I make this do?"', 845.085, 848.909, NULL),
  (26513, 132, 'I''m going to take all the screws out,
and take the back off,', 849.102, 852.029, NULL),
  (26514, 132, 'and break it into a lot of little pieces.', 852.029, 853.984, NULL),
  (26515, 132, 'But then I''m going to figure out
what I can build from the rubble.', 853.984, 857.343, NULL),
  (26516, 132, 'That''s discovery, and we need to do that
in science and technology', 857.343, 861.299, NULL),
  (26517, 132, 'to figure out what''s possible.', 861.299, 863.439, NULL),
  (26518, 132, 'And so in the lab what I''m trying
to do is apply that mindset', 863.439, 867.118, NULL),
  (26519, 132, 'to some of the biggest
problems humans have.', 867.118, 869.583, NULL),
  (26520, 132, 'We work on malaria, thanks to
Bill Gates, who asked us to work on it.', 869.583, 874.152, NULL),
  (26521, 132, 'This is how we used to solve malaria.', 874.152, 876.863, NULL),
  (26522, 132, 'This is a real ad from like the 40''s.', 876.863, 879.070, NULL),
  (26523, 132, 'We eradicated malaria in the US
by spraying DDT everywhere.', 879.070, 883.205, NULL),
  (26524, 132, 'In the lab what we do is a lot of work
to try and understand the problem.', 884.455, 888.505, NULL),
  (26525, 132, 'This is a high-speed video,
we have a badass video camera,', 888.505, 893.658, NULL),
  (26526, 132, 'trying to learn how mosquitos fly.', 893.658, 896.293, NULL),
  (26527, 132, 'And you can see that
they''re more like swimming in air.', 896.293, 899.441, NULL),
  (26528, 132, 'We actually have no idea how they fly.', 899.441, 901.299, NULL),
  (26529, 132, 'But we have a cool video camera so we -', 901.299, 903.520, NULL),
  (26530, 132, '(Laughter)', 903.520, 905.534, NULL),
  (26531, 132, 'Yeah, it cost more than a Ferrari.', 905.534, 909.245, NULL),
  (26532, 132, 'Anyway we came up with some
ways to take care of mosquitos.', 909.245, 912.395, NULL),
  (26533, 132, 'Let''s shoot them down with laser beams.', 912.395, 914.807, NULL),
  (26534, 132, 'This is what happens when you put
one of every kind of scientist in a room', 914.807, 919.318, NULL),
  (26535, 132, 'and a laser junky.', 919.318, 921.318, NULL),
  (26536, 132, 'So people thought it was funny at first,', 921.318, 925.237, NULL),
  (26537, 132, 'but we figured out, you know, we can
build this out of consumer electronics.', 925.237, 930.076, NULL),
  (26538, 132, 'It''s using the CCD from a webcam,', 930.076, 933.390, NULL),
  (26539, 132, 'the laser from a Blu-ray burner,', 933.390, 936.590, NULL),
  (26540, 132, 'the laser galvo is from a laser printer.', 936.590, 940.212, NULL),
  (26541, 132, 'We do motion detection on a GPU processor', 940.212, 943.220, NULL),
  (26542, 132, 'like you might find in video game system.', 943.220, 945.414, NULL),
  (26543, 132, 'It''s all stuff that follows Moore''s law.', 945.414, 947.343, NULL),
  (26544, 132, 'So it''s actually not going to
be that expensive to do it.', 947.343, 950.228, NULL),
  (26545, 132, 'The idea is that we would put', 950.228, 952.466, NULL),
  (26546, 132, 'a perimeter of these laser systems
around a building or a village', 952.466, 956.317, NULL),
  (26547, 132, 'and just shoot all the mosquitos
on their way in to feed on humans.', 956.317, 959.507, NULL),
  (26548, 132, 'And we might want to do that
for your backyard.', 959.507, 962.800, NULL),
  (26549, 132, 'We could also do it to protect crops.', 962.800, 964.763, NULL),
  (26550, 132, 'Our team is right now working on', 964.763, 966.629, NULL),
  (26551, 132, 'characterizing what they
need to do the same thing for', 966.629, 969.285, NULL),
  (26552, 132, 'the pest that has wiped out
about two thirds', 969.285, 972.899, NULL),
  (26553, 132, 'of the Orange groves in Florida.', 972.899, 976.477, NULL),
  (26554, 132, 'So people laughed at first.', 978.102, 980.719, NULL),
  (26555, 132, 'This is a video of our system working.', 980.719, 983.441, NULL),
  (26556, 132, 'We are tracking mosquitos live
as they fly around.', 983.441, 986.119, NULL),
  (26557, 132, 'Those crosshairs are put there
by our computer.', 986.119, 988.622, NULL),
  (26558, 132, 'It just watches them, finds them moving', 988.622, 990.483, NULL),
  (26559, 132, 'and then it aims a laser at them
to sample their wing beat frequency.', 990.483, 994.217, NULL),
  (26560, 132, 'Figure out from that, is this a mosquito?', 994.217, 997.424, NULL),
  (26561, 132, 'Is it Anopheles Stephensi?
Is it female?', 997.424, 1000.325, NULL),
  (26562, 132, 'And if all that''s true then
we shoot it down with lethal laser.', 1000.325, 1004.912, NULL),
  (26563, 132, '(Laughter)', 1004.912, 1006.981, NULL),
  (26564, 132, 'So we have this working in a lab.', 1006.981, 1008.753, NULL),
  (26565, 132, 'We''re working on taking
that project into the field now.', 1008.753, 1011.879, NULL),
  (26566, 132, 'All this happens at the Intellectual
Ventures Lab in Seattle where I work', 1011.879, 1016.425, NULL),
  (26567, 132, 'and we try and take on some
of the hardest problems that humans have.', 1016.425, 1021.626, NULL),
  (26568, 132, 'This is the money shot.', 1021.626, 1023.468, NULL),
  (26569, 132, 'You can see we just burned
