  (26584, 133, 'Transcriber: Linda Anderson
Reviewer: Rebecca DeHovitz', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (26585, 133, 'So, I have a Facebook friend
whose life seems perfect.', 4.465, 9.390, NULL),
  (26586, 133, 'She lives in a gorgeous house.', 9.390, 11.770, NULL),
  (26587, 133, 'And she has a really rewarding career.', 11.770, 14.456, NULL),
  (26588, 133, 'And she and her family go', 14.456, 15.665, NULL),
  (26589, 133, 'on all these exciting adventures
together on the weekends.', 15.665, 19.266, NULL),
  (26590, 133, 'And I swear that they must take', 19.266, 20.776, NULL),
  (26591, 133, 'a professional photographer
along with them,', 20.776, 22.876, NULL),
  (26592, 133, '(Laughter)', 22.876, 24.233, NULL),
  (26593, 133, 'because no matter where they go
or what they do,', 24.233, 26.563, NULL),
  (26594, 133, 'the whole family just looks beautiful.', 26.563, 29.502, NULL),
  (26595, 133, 'And she''s always posting 
about how blessed she is,', 29.502, 33.271, NULL),
  (26596, 133, 'and how grateful she is
for the life that she has.', 33.271, 36.271, NULL),
  (26597, 133, 'And I get the feeling
that she''s not just saying those things', 36.271, 39.177, NULL),
  (26598, 133, 'for the sake of Facebook,
but she truly means it.', 39.177, 43.514, NULL),
  (26599, 133, 'How many of you have a friend
kind of like that?', 43.514, 48.558, NULL),
  (26600, 133, 'And how many of you', 48.558, 50.513, NULL),
  (26601, 133, 'kind of don''t like that person sometimes?', 50.513, 53.413, NULL),
  (26602, 133, '(Laughter)', 53.413, 56.215, NULL),
  (26603, 133, 'We all do this, right?', 56.215, 58.802, NULL),
  (26604, 133, 'It''s hard not to do.', 58.802, 60.745, NULL),
  (26605, 133, 'But that way of thinking 
costs us something.', 60.745, 64.548, NULL),
  (26606, 133, 'And that''s what I want to talk
to you about today--', 64.548, 66.964, NULL),
  (26607, 133, 'is what our bad habits cost us.', 66.964, 70.875, NULL),
  (26608, 133, 'Maybe you''ve scrolled through
your Facebook feed', 70.875, 73.217, NULL),
  (26609, 133, 'and you think, "So what
if I roll my eyes?', 73.217, 75.693, NULL),
  (26610, 133, 'It''s just five seconds of my time.', 75.693, 78.219, NULL),
  (26611, 133, 'How could it be hurting me?"', 78.219, 80.582, NULL),
  (26612, 133, 'Well, researchers have found ', 80.582, 82.249, NULL),
  (26613, 133, 'that envying your friends on Facebook,', 82.249, 85.211, NULL),
  (26614, 133, 'actually leads to depression.', 85.211, 88.081, NULL),
  (26615, 133, 'That''s just one of the traps
that our minds can set for us.', 88.081, 92.022, NULL),
  (26616, 133, 'Have you ever complained about your boss?', 92.022, 95.457, NULL),
  (26617, 133, 'Or looked at your friends''
lives and thought,', 95.457, 97.794, NULL),
  (26618, 133, '"Why do they have all the luck?"', 97.794, 100.472, NULL),
  (26619, 133, 'You can''t help thinking that way, right?', 100.472, 103.033, NULL),
  (26620, 133, 'That way of thinking seems
small in the moment.', 103.033, 105.856, NULL),
  (26621, 133, 'In fact, it might even make you feel
better in the moment.', 105.856, 109.692, NULL),
  (26622, 133, 'But that way of thinking is
eating away at your mental strength.', 109.692, 115.054, NULL),
  (26623, 133, 'There''s three kinds of destructive beliefs', 115.054, 117.772, NULL),
  (26624, 133, 'that make us less effective,', 117.772, 119.846, NULL),
  (26625, 133, 'and rob us of our mental strength.', 119.846, 123.056, NULL),
  (26626, 133, 'The first one is unhealthy
beliefs about ourselves.', 123.056, 127.852, NULL),
  (26627, 133, 'We tend to feel sorry for ourselves.', 127.852, 130.715, NULL),
  (26628, 133, 'And while it''s OK to be sad
when something bad happens,', 130.715, 134.423, NULL),
  (26629, 133, 'self-pity goes beyond that.', 134.423, 136.220, NULL),
  (26630, 133, 'It''s when you start
to magnify your misfortune.', 136.220, 139.078, NULL),
  (26631, 133, 'When you think things like,', 139.078, 140.668, NULL),
  (26632, 133, '"Why do these things
always have to happen to me?"', 140.668, 143.041, NULL),
  (26633, 133, '"I shouldn''t have to deal with it."', 143.041, 145.884, NULL),
  (26634, 133, 'That way of thinking keeps you stuck,', 145.884, 147.762, NULL),
  (26635, 133, 'keeps you focused on the problem,', 147.762, 149.888, NULL),
  (26636, 133, 'keeps you from finding a solution.', 149.888, 153.158, NULL),
  (26637, 133, 'And even when you can''t create a solution,', 153.158, 155.251, NULL),
  (26638, 133, 'you can always take steps to make
your life or somebody else''s life better.', 155.251, 159.462, NULL),
  (26639, 133, 'But you can''t do that', 159.462, 160.650, NULL),
  (26640, 133, 'when you''re busy
hosting your own pity party.', 160.650, 165.160, NULL),
  (26641, 133, 'The second type of destructive
belief that holds us back', 165.160, 168.811, NULL),
  (26642, 133, 'is unhealthy beliefs about others.', 168.811, 172.075, NULL),
  (26643, 133, 'We think that other people can control us,', 172.075, 174.510, NULL),
  (26644, 133, 'and we give away our power.', 174.510, 177.850, NULL),
  (26645, 133, 'But as adults who live in a free country,', 177.850, 180.697, NULL),
  (26646, 133, 'there''s very few things in life
that you have to do.', 180.697, 184.476, NULL),
  (26647, 133, 'So when you say, "I have to work late,"', 184.476, 187.258, NULL),
  (26648, 133, 'you give away your power.', 187.258, 189.448, NULL),
  (26649, 133, 'Yeah, maybe there will be
consequences if you don''t work late,', 189.448, 192.370, NULL),
  (26650, 133, 'but it''s still a choice.', 192.370, 195.675, NULL),
  (26651, 133, 'Or when you say, "My
mother-in-law drives me crazy,"', 195.675, 199.760, NULL),
  (26652, 133, 'you give away your power.', 199.760, 202.256, NULL),
  (26653, 133, 'Maybe she''s not the nicest 
person on earth,', 202.256, 205.169, NULL),
  (26654, 133, 'but it''s up to you how you respond to her,', 205.169, 207.194, NULL),
  (26655, 133, 'because you''re in control.', 207.194, 211.424, NULL),
  (26656, 133, 'The third type of unhealthy
belief that holds us back,', 211.424, 215.021, NULL),
  (26657, 133, 'is unhealthy beliefs about the world.', 215.021, 218.531, NULL),
  (26658, 133, 'We tend to think that the world
owes us something.', 218.531, 221.293, NULL),
  (26659, 133, 'We think, "If I put in enough hard work,', 221.293, 224.075, NULL),
  (26660, 133, 'then I deserve success."', 224.075, 227.075, NULL),
  (26661, 133, 'But expecting success
to fall into your lap', 227.075, 229.261, NULL),
  (26662, 133, 'like some sort of cosmic reward,', 229.261, 232.209, NULL),
  (26663, 133, 'will only lead to disappointment.', 232.209, 236.429, NULL),
  (26664, 133, 'But I know it''s hard to give up
our bad mental habits.', 236.429, 239.378, NULL),
  (26665, 133, 'It''s hard to get rid of those 
unhealthy beliefs', 239.378, 241.628, NULL),
  (26666, 133, 'that we''ve carried around
with us for so long.', 241.628, 244.729, NULL),
  (26667, 133, 'But you can''t afford not to give them up.', 244.729, 247.850, NULL),
  (26668, 133, 'Because sooner or later, you''re
going to hit a time in your life', 247.850, 251.484, NULL),
  (26669, 133, 'where you need all the mental 
strength that you can muster.', 251.484, 256.906, NULL),
  (26670, 133, 'When I was 23 years old,', 256.906, 259.066, NULL),
  (26671, 133, 'I thought I had life all figured out.', 259.066, 263.006, NULL),
  (26672, 133, 'I graduated from grad school.', 263.006, 265.160, NULL),
  (26673, 133, 'I landed my first big job as a therapist.', 265.160, 268.464, NULL),
  (26674, 133, 'I got married.', 268.464, 269.670, NULL),
  (26675, 133, 'And I even bought a house.', 269.675, 271.356, NULL),
  (26676, 133, 'And I thought,
"This is going to be great!"', 271.356, 273.356, NULL),
  (26677, 133, '"I''ve got this incredible
jump start on success."', 273.356, 276.461, NULL),
  (26678, 133, 'What could go wrong?', 276.461, 279.498, NULL),
  (26679, 133, 'That all changed for me one day', 279.498, 281.463, NULL),
  (26680, 133, 'when I got a phone call from my sister.', 281.463, 284.573, NULL),
  (26681, 133, 'She said that our mother
was found unresponsive', 284.573, 287.862, NULL),
  (26682, 133, 'and she''d been taken to the hospital.', 287.862, 290.798, NULL),
  (26683, 133, 'My husband Lincoln and I jumped 
in the car and rushed to the hospital.', 290.798, 294.926, NULL),
  (26684, 133, 'We couldn''t imagine what could be wrong.', 294.926, 297.497, NULL),
  (26685, 133, 'My mother was only 51.', 297.497, 299.320, NULL),
  (26686, 133, 'She didn''t have any history
of any kind of health problems.', 299.322, 304.431, NULL),
  (26687, 133, 'When we got to the hospital,', 304.431, 305.895, NULL),
  (26688, 133, 'doctors explained she''d had
a brain aneurysm.', 305.895, 310.068, NULL),
  (26689, 133, 'And within 24 hours, my mother,', 310.068, 313.019, NULL),
  (26690, 133, 'who used to wake up in the morning
saying, "It''s a great day to be alive,"', 313.019, 317.235, NULL),
  (26691, 133, 'passed away.', 317.235, 319.480, NULL),
  (26692, 133, 'That news was devastating to me.', 319.480, 321.233, NULL),
  (26693, 133, 'My mother and I had been very close.', 321.233, 323.893, NULL),
  (26694, 133, 'As a therapist, I knew on an intellectual
level how to go through grief.', 323.893, 328.284, NULL),
  (26695, 133, 'But knowing it, and doing it, 
can be two very different things.', 328.284, 332.872, NULL),
  (26696, 133, 'It took a long time before I felt
like I was really healing.', 332.872, 338.208, NULL),
  (26697, 133, 'And then on the three year anniversary
of my mother''s death,', 338.208, 342.503, NULL),
  (26698, 133, 'some friends called,', 342.503, 344.194, NULL),
  (26699, 133, 'and invited Lincoln and me
to a basketball game.', 344.194, 348.474, NULL),
  (26700, 133, 'Coincidentally, it was being played', 348.474, 350.780, NULL),
  (26701, 133, 'at the same auditorium
where I''d last seen my mother,', 350.780, 354.389, NULL),
  (26702, 133, 'on the night before she''d passed away.', 354.389, 357.442, NULL),
  (26703, 133, 'I hadn''t been back there since.', 357.442, 359.487, NULL),
  (26704, 133, 'I wasn''t even sure I wanted to go back.', 359.487, 361.923, NULL),
  (26705, 133, 'But Lincoln and I talked about it,
and ultimately we said,', 361.923, 365.413, NULL),
  (26706, 133, '"Maybe that would be a good way
to honor her memory."', 365.413, 368.466, NULL),
  (26707, 133, 'So we went to the game.', 368.466, 370.324, NULL),
  (26708, 133, 'And we actually had a really good
time with our friends.', 370.324, 373.492, NULL),
  (26709, 133, 'On the drive home that night,', 373.492, 375.172, NULL),
  (26710, 133, 'we talked about how great it was', 375.172, 376.714, NULL),
  (26711, 133, 'to finally be able to go
back to that place,', 376.714, 379.060, NULL),
  (26712, 133, 'and remember my mother with a smile,', 379.060, 381.247, NULL),
  (26713, 133, 'rather than all those feelings of sadness.', 381.247, 385.837, NULL),
  (26714, 133, 'But shortly after we got home that night, 
Lincoln said he didn''t feel well.', 385.837, 391.206, NULL),
  (26715, 133, 'A few minutes later, he collapsed.', 391.206, 394.546, NULL),
  (26716, 133, 'I had to call for an ambulance.', 394.546, 397.849, NULL),
  (26717, 133, 'His family met me at the emergency room.', 397.849, 400.626, NULL),
  (26718, 133, 'We waited for what seemed like forever,', 400.626, 403.698, NULL),
  (26719, 133, 'until finally a doctor came out.', 403.698, 406.698, NULL),
  (26720, 133, 'But rather than taking
us out back to see Lincoln,', 406.698, 409.652, NULL),
  (26721, 133, 'he took us back to a private room,', 409.652, 413.482, NULL),
  (26722, 133, 'and sat us down,', 413.482, 415.272, NULL),
  (26723, 133, 'and explained to us that Lincoln,', 415.272, 417.100, NULL),
  (26724, 133, 'who was the most adventurous
person I''d ever met,', 417.100, 419.950, NULL),
  (26725, 133, 'was gone.', 419.950, 423.250, NULL),
  (26726, 133, 'We didn''t know at the time, 
but he''d had a heart attack.', 423.250, 426.575, NULL),
  (26727, 133, 'He was only 26.', 426.575, 428.977, NULL),
  (26728, 133, 'He didn''t have any history
of heart problems.', 428.977, 434.025, NULL),
  (26729, 133, 'So now I found myself a 26-year-old widow,', 434.025, 437.020, NULL),
  (26730, 133, 'and I didn''t have my mom.', 437.020, 439.660, NULL),
  (26731, 133, 'I thought, "How am I going
to get through this/"', 439.660, 442.586, NULL),
  (26732, 133, 'And to describe that
as a painful period in my life', 442.586, 445.274, NULL),
  (26733, 133, 'feels like an understatement.', 445.274, 447.514, NULL),
  (26734, 133, 'And it was during that time
that I realized', 447.514, 449.680, NULL),
  (26735, 133, 'when you''re really going
through tough times,', 449.680, 451.867, NULL),
  (26736, 133, 'good habits aren''t enough.', 451.867, 454.047, NULL),
  (26737, 133, 'It only takes one or two small habits', 454.047, 457.270, NULL),
  (26738, 133, 'to really hold you back.', 457.270, 460.020, NULL),
  (26739, 133, 'I worked as hard as I could,', 460.020, 461.970, NULL),
  (26740, 133, 'not just to create good habits in my life,', 461.970, 464.001, NULL),
  (26741, 133, 'but to get rid of those small habits,', 464.001, 466.241, NULL),
  (26742, 133, 'no matter how small they might seem.', 466.241, 469.261, NULL),
  (26743, 133, 'Throughout it all,', 469.261, 470.523, NULL),
  (26744, 133, 'I held out hope that someday
life could get better.', 470.523, 474.763, NULL),
  (26745, 133, 'And eventually it did.', 474.763, 477.215, NULL),
  (26746, 133, 'A few years down the road, I met Steve.', 477.215, 479.556, NULL),
  (26747, 133, 'And we fell in love.', 479.556, 481.266, NULL),
  (26748, 133, 'And I got remarried.', 481.266, 483.560, NULL),
  (26749, 133, 'We sold the house that
Lincoln and I had lived in,', 483.560, 485.960, NULL),
  (26750, 133, 'and we bought a new house, in a new area,', 485.960, 489.159, NULL),
  (26751, 133, 'and I got a new job.', 489.159, 492.159, NULL),
  (26752, 133, 'But almost as quickly
as I breathed my sigh of relief', 492.159, 495.098, NULL),
  (26753, 133, 'over that fresh start that I had,', 495.098, 497.944, NULL),
  (26754, 133, 'we got the news that Steve''s dad
had terminal cancer.', 497.951, 502.970, NULL),
  (26755, 133, 'And I started to think,', 502.970, 504.180, NULL),
  (26756, 133, '"Why do these things always
have to keep happening?"', 504.180, 506.612, NULL),
  (26757, 133, '"Why do I have to keep losing
all my loved ones?"', 506.612, 509.023, NULL),
  (26758, 133, '"This isn''t fair."', 509.023, 513.099, NULL),
  (26759, 133, 'But if I''d learned anything,', 513.099, 514.856, NULL),
  (26760, 133, 'it was that that way of thinking
would hold me back.', 514.856, 519.653, NULL),
  (26761, 133, 'I knew I was going to need', 519.653, 521.043, NULL),
  (26762, 133, 'as much mental strength as I could muster,', 521.043, 523.332, NULL),
  (26763, 133, 'to get through one more loss.', 523.332, 526.463, NULL),
  (26764, 133, 'So I sat down and I wrote a list', 526.463, 528.531, NULL),
  (26765, 133, 'of all the things mentally
strong people don''t do.', 528.531, 532.703, NULL),
  (26766, 133, 'And I read over that list.', 532.703, 534.243, NULL),
  (26767, 133, 'It was a reminder of all
of those bad habits', 534.243, 536.804, NULL),
  (26768, 133, 'that I''d done at one time or another, 
that would keep me stuck.', 536.804, 541.103, NULL),
  (26769, 133, 'And I kept reading
that list over and over.', 541.103, 543.682, NULL),
  (26770, 133, 'And I really needed it.', 543.682, 545.415, NULL),
  (26771, 133, 'Because within a few weeks of writing it,', 545.415, 547.978, NULL),
  (26772, 133, 'Steve''s dad passed away.', 547.978, 552.968, NULL),
  (26773, 133, 'My journey taught me that the secret
to being mentally strong,', 552.968, 557.407, NULL),
  (26774, 133, 'was that you had to give up
your bad mental habits.', 557.407, 561.222, NULL),
  (26775, 133, 'Mental strength is a lot
like physical strength.', 561.222, 564.068, NULL),
  (26776, 133, 'If you wanted to be physically strong,', 564.068, 566.563, NULL),
  (26777, 133, 'you''d need to go to the gym
and lift weights.', 566.563, 569.064, NULL),
  (26778, 133, 'But if you really wanted to see results,', 569.064, 571.932, NULL),
  (26779, 133, 'you''d also have to give up
eating junk food.', 571.932, 575.000, NULL),
  (26780, 133, 'Mental strength is the same.', 575.000, 576.383, NULL),
  (26781, 133, 'If you want to be mentally strong,', 576.383, 578.229, NULL),
  (26782, 133, 'you need good habits
like practicing gratitude.', 578.229, 581.935, NULL),
  (26783, 133, 'But you also have to give up bad habits,', 581.935, 583.866, NULL),
  (26784, 133, 'like resenting somebody else''s success.', 583.866, 587.266, NULL),
  (26785, 133, 'No matter how often that happens,', 587.266, 589.693, NULL),
  (26786, 133, 'it will hold you back.', 589.693, 593.263, NULL),
  (26787, 133, 'So, how do you train
your brain to think differently?', 593.263, 597.279, NULL),
  (26788, 133, 'How do you give up those bad mental habits', 597.279, 600.291, NULL),
  (26789, 133, 'that you''ve carried around with you?', 600.291, 603.091, NULL),
  (26790, 133, 'It starts by countering those
unhealthy beliefs that I talked about,', 603.091, 607.534, NULL),
  (26791, 133, 'with healthier ones.', 607.534, 610.749, NULL),
  (26792, 133, 'For example, unhealthy
beliefs about ourselves', 610.749, 613.879, NULL),
  (26793, 133, 'mostly come about because we''re 
uncomfortable with our feelings.', 613.879, 617.408, NULL),
  (26794, 133, 'Feeling sad, or hurt, or angry, or scared,', 617.408, 619.985, NULL),
  (26795, 133, 'those things are all uncomfortable.', 619.985, 622.507, NULL),
  (26796, 133, 'So we go to great lengths
to avoid that discomfort.', 622.507, 625.777, NULL),
  (26797, 133, 'We try to escape it', 625.777, 628.155, NULL),
  (26798, 133, 'by doing things like hosting a pity party.', 628.155, 631.855, NULL),
  (26799, 133, 'And although that''s
a temporary distraction,', 631.855, 634.456, NULL),
  (26800, 133, 'it just prolongs the pain.', 634.456, 636.646, NULL),
  (26801, 133, 'The only way to get through 
uncomfortable emotions,', 636.646, 639.625, NULL),
  (26802, 133, 'the only way to deal with them,
is you have to go through them.', 639.625, 642.697, NULL),
  (26803, 133, 'To let yourself feel sad,
and then move on.', 642.697, 646.261, NULL),
  (26804, 133, 'To gain confidence in your ability', 646.261, 647.952, NULL),
  (26805, 133, 'to deal with that discomfort.', 647.952, 651.852, NULL),
  (26806, 133, 'Unhealthy beliefs about others come about', 651.852, 654.659, NULL),
  (26807, 133, 'because we compare
ourselves to other people.', 654.659, 657.675, NULL),
  (26808, 133, 'We think that they''re
either above us or below us.', 657.675, 660.653, NULL),
  (26809, 133, 'Or we think that they can
control how we feel.', 660.659, 662.866, NULL),
  (26810, 133, 'Or that we can control how they behave.', 662.866, 665.214, NULL),
  (26811, 133, 'Or we blame them for holding us back.', 665.214, 667.906, NULL),
  (26812, 133, 'But really, it''s our own
choices that do that.', 667.906, 671.354, NULL),
  (26813, 133, 'You have to accept
that you''re your own person,', 671.354, 673.560, NULL),
  (26814, 133, 'and other people are separate from you.', 673.560, 676.034, NULL),
  (26815, 133, 'The only person you should
compare yourself to,', 676.034, 678.299, NULL),
  (26816, 133, 'is the person that you were yesterday.', 678.299, 682.302, NULL),
  (26817, 133, 'And unhealthy beliefs
about the world come about', 682.302, 685.169, NULL),
  (26818, 133, 'because deep down,
we want the world to be fair.', 685.169, 689.033, NULL),
  (26819, 133, 'We want to think that if we
put in enough good deeds,', 689.033, 692.510, NULL),
  (26820, 133, 'enough good things will happen to us.', 692.510, 694.767, NULL),
  (26821, 133, 'Or if we tough it out
through enough bad times,', 694.767, 697.424, NULL),
  (26822, 133, 'we''ll get some sort of reward.', 697.424, 700.424, NULL),
  (26823, 133, 'But ultimately you have
to accept that life isn''t fair.', 700.424, 704.556, NULL),
  (26824, 133, 'And that can be liberating.', 704.556, 706.548, NULL),
  (26825, 133, 'Yeah, it means you won''t necessarily
be rewarded for your goodness,', 706.548, 710.079, NULL),
  (26826, 133, 'but it also means no matter
how much you''ve suffered,', 710.083, 712.860, NULL),
  (26827, 133, 'you''re not doomed to keep suffering.', 712.860, 716.502, NULL),
  (26828, 133, 'The world doesn''t work that way.', 716.502, 719.201, NULL),
  (26829, 133, 'Your world is what you make it.', 719.201, 722.641, NULL),
  (26830, 133, 'But of course before you
can change your world,', 722.641, 725.017, NULL),
  (26831, 133, 'you have to believe
that you can change it.', 725.017, 728.845, NULL),
  (26832, 133, 'I once worked with this man
who had been diabetic for years.', 728.845, 733.237, NULL),
  (26833, 133, 'His doctor referred him to therapy', 733.237, 735.446, NULL),
  (26834, 133, 'because he had some bad mental habits', 735.446, 737.716, NULL),
  (26835, 133, 'that were starting to affect
his physical health.', 737.716, 741.176, NULL),
  (26836, 133, 'His mother had died from complications
of diabetes at a young age,', 741.176, 745.239, NULL),
  (26837, 133, 'so he just believed he was doomed,', 745.239, 747.693, NULL),
  (26838, 133, 'and he''d given up trying to manage
his blood sugar altogether.', 747.693, 751.831, NULL),
  (26839, 133, 'In fact, his blood sugar
had gotten so high lately,', 751.831, 754.785, NULL),
  (26840, 133, 'that it was starting to affect his vision.', 754.785, 757.381, NULL),
  (26841, 133, 'And he had his driver''s
license taken away.', 757.381, 760.381, NULL),
  (26842, 133, 'And his world was shrinking.', 760.381, 764.129, NULL),
  (26843, 133, 'When he came into my office, it was clear', 764.129, 766.491, NULL),
  (26844, 133, 'he knew all the things
he could do to manage his blood sugar.', 766.491, 770.199, NULL),
  (26845, 133, 'He just didn''t think
it was worth the effort.', 770.201, 774.221, NULL),
  (26846, 133, 'But eventually, he agreed
to make one small change.', 774.221, 778.911, NULL),
  (26847, 133, 'He said, "I''ll give up
my two liter-a-day Pepsi habit,', 778.911, 782.322, NULL),
  (26848, 133, 'and I''ll trade it in for Diet Pepsi."', 782.322, 785.135, NULL),
  (26849, 133, 'And he couldn''t believe how quickly
his numbers started to improve.', 785.142, 790.633, NULL),
  (26850, 133, 'And even though he came every week', 790.633, 792.455, NULL),
  (26851, 133, 'to remind me how horrible
Diet Pepsi tasted,', 792.455, 796.621, NULL),
  (26852, 133, 'he stuck with it.', 796.621, 799.571, NULL),
  (26853, 133, 'And once he started to see
a little bit of improvement,', 799.571, 802.181, NULL),
  (26854, 133, 'he said, "Well, maybe I could
look at some of my other habits."', 802.181, 805.934, NULL),
  (26855, 133, 'He said, "I could trade in
my nightly bowl of ice cream', 805.934, 808.935, NULL),
  (26856, 133, 'for a snack with a little less sugar."', 808.935, 812.180, NULL),
  (26857, 133, 'And then one day he was at a thrift
store with some friends,', 812.180, 815.776, NULL),
  (26858, 133, 'and he found this beat-up
old exercise bike.', 815.776, 818.678, NULL),
  (26859, 133, 'He bought it for a couple of bucks,', 818.678, 820.722, NULL),
  (26860, 133, 'and he brought it home,
and he parked it in front of his TV.', 820.722, 824.223, NULL),
  (26861, 133, 'And he started to pedal', 824.223, 825.417, NULL),
  (26862, 133, 'while he''d watch some
of his favorite shows every night.', 825.417, 829.477, NULL),
  (26863, 133, 'And not only did he lose weight,', 829.477, 831.780, NULL),
  (26864, 133, 'but one day, he noticed
he could see the TV', 831.780, 835.590, NULL),
  (26865, 133, 'just a little bit more clearly
than he had before.', 835.590, 839.784, NULL),
  (26866, 133, 'And suddenly it occurred to him,', 839.784, 841.872, NULL),
  (26867, 133, 'maybe the damage done
to his eyesight wasn''t permanent.', 841.875, 846.642, NULL),
  (26868, 133, 'So he set a new goal for himself--', 846.642, 848.328, NULL),
  (26869, 133, 'to get his driver''s license back.', 848.328, 851.238, NULL),
  (26870, 133, 'And from that day forward, he was on fire.', 851.238, 854.709, NULL),
  (26871, 133, 'By the end of our time together,
he was coming in every week', 854.709, 857.584, NULL),
  (26872, 133, 'saying, "OK, what are we
going to do this week?"', 857.584, 861.015, NULL),
  (26873, 133, 'Because he finally believed
that he could change his world.', 861.015, 864.541, NULL),
  (26874, 133, 'And that he had the mental
strength to change it.', 864.541, 867.798, NULL),
  (26875, 133, 'And that he could give up
his bad mental habits.', 867.798, 870.334, NULL),
  (26876, 133, 'And it all started
with just one small step.', 870.334, 875.680, NULL),
  (26877, 133, 'So I invite you to consider', 875.680, 877.679, NULL),
  (26878, 133, 'what bad mental habits
are holding you back?', 877.679, 881.559, NULL),
  (26879, 133, 'What unhealthy beliefs', 881.559, 883.168, NULL),
  (26880, 133, 'are keeping you from being
as mentally strong as you could be?', 883.168, 887.882, NULL),
  (26881, 133, 'And what is one small step
that you could take today?', 887.882, 891.485, NULL),
  (26882, 133, 'Right here, right now.', 891.485, 894.574, NULL),
  (26883, 133, 'Thank you.', 894.574, 895.906, NULL),
  (26884, 133, '(Applause)', 895.906, 897.767, NULL),
  (26885, 134, 'Transcriber: Ilze Garda
Reviewer: Denise RQ', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (26886, 134, 'In this talk, I''m going to give you
the single most important lesson', 7.375, 13.333, NULL),
  (26887, 134, 'my colleagues and I have learned
from looking at 83,000 brain scans.', 13.334, 18.751, NULL),
  (26888, 134, 'But first, let me put
the lesson into context.', 19.331, 23.386, NULL),
  (26889, 134, 'I am in the middle of seven children.', 23.387, 25.874, NULL),
  (26890, 134, 'Growing up, my father called me a maverick', 25.875, 29.202, NULL),
  (26891, 134, 'which to him was not a good thing.', 29.203, 32.473, NULL),
  (26892, 134, '(Laughter)', 32.475, 33.862, NULL),
  (26893, 134, 'In 1972, the army called my number,', 33.863, 37.279, NULL),
  (26894, 134, 'and I was trained as an infantry medic
where my love of medicine was born.', 37.280, 42.376, NULL),
  (26895, 134, 'But since I truly hated the idea
of being shot at or sleeping in the mud,', 43.284, 49.711, NULL),
  (26896, 134, 'I got myself retrained
as an X-ray technician', 50.331, 53.731, NULL),
  (26897, 134, 'and developed a passion
for medical imaging.', 53.732, 57.687, NULL),
  (26898, 134, 'As our professors used to say:
"How do you know, unless you look?"', 57.688, 62.823, NULL),
  (26899, 134, 'In 1979, when I was
a second-year medical student,', 63.393, 67.217, NULL),
  (26900, 134, 'someone in my family
became seriously suicidal,', 67.218, 71.286, NULL),
  (26901, 134, 'and I took her to see
a wonderful psychiatrist.', 72.136, 74.678, NULL),
  (26902, 134, 'Over time, I realized
if he helped her, which he did,', 75.148, 80.896, NULL),
  (26903, 134, 'it would not only save her life,', 80.897, 84.003, NULL),
  (26904, 134, 'but it would also help her children
and even her future grandchildren,', 84.004, 89.689, NULL),
  (26905, 134, 'as they would be shaped by someone
who is happier and more stable.', 89.690, 95.942, NULL),
  (26906, 134, 'I fell in love with psychiatry', 96.505, 98.763, NULL),
  (26907, 134, 'because I realized it had the potential
to change generations of people.', 98.764, 105.363, NULL),
  (26908, 134, 'In 1991, I went to my first lecture
on brain SPECT imaging.', 107.000, 111.334, NULL),
  (26909, 134, 'SPECT is a nuclear medicine study
that looks at the blood flow and activity,', 111.353, 116.836, NULL),
  (26910, 134, 'it looks at how your brain works.', 116.837, 120.168, NULL),
  (26911, 134, 'SPECT was presented
as a tool to help psychiatrists', 120.748, 124.193, NULL),
  (26912, 134, 'get more information
to help their patients.', 124.194, 128.896, NULL),
  (26913, 134, 'In that one lecture,
my two professional loves,', 129.538, 133.337, NULL),
  (26914, 134, 'medical imaging and psychiatry,', 133.338, 135.829, NULL),
  (26915, 134, 'came together, and quite honestly,
revolutionized my life.', 135.830, 140.505, NULL),
  (26916, 134, 'Over the next 22 years,
my colleagues and I would build', 141.045, 144.977, NULL),
  (26917, 134, 'the world''s largest database
of brain scans related to behavior', 144.978, 149.609, NULL),
  (26918, 134, 'on patients from 93 countries.', 149.610, 152.854, NULL),
  (26919, 134, 'SPECT basically tells us
three things about the brain:', 153.592, 157.528, NULL),
  (26920, 134, 'good activity, too little, or too much.', 157.529, 161.071, NULL),
  (26921, 134, 'Here''s a set of healthy SPECT scans.', 161.072, 163.756, NULL),
  (26922, 134, 'The image on the left shows
the outside surface of the brain,', 163.757, 168.199, NULL),
  (26923, 134, 'and a healthy scan shows full,
even, symmetrical activity.', 168.200, 173.176, NULL),
  (26924, 134, 'The color is not important,
it''s the shape that matters.', 173.177, 178.146, NULL),
  (26925, 134, 'In the image on the right,
red equals the areas of high activity,', 178.147, 183.521, NULL),
  (26926, 134, 'and in a healthy brain, they''re typically
in the back part of the brain.', 183.522, 188.837, NULL),
  (26927, 134, 'Here''s a healthy scan compared
to someone who had two strokes.', 190.241, 194.128, NULL),
  (26928, 134, 'You can see the holes of activity.', 194.129, 196.796, NULL),
  (26929, 134, 'Here''s what Alzheimer''s looks like,', 197.502, 199.284, NULL),
  (26930, 134, 'where the back half
of the brain is deteriorating.', 199.285, 203.108, NULL),
  (26931, 134, 'Did you know that Alzheimer''s disease
actually starts in the brain', 203.109, 208.419, NULL),
  (26932, 134, '30 to 50 years before
you have any symptoms?', 208.420, 213.014, NULL),
  (26933, 134, 'Here''s a scan
of a traumatic brain injury.', 214.171, 216.514, NULL),
  (26934, 134, 'Your brain is soft,
and your skull is really hard.', 216.515, 220.232, NULL),
  (26935, 134, 'Or drug abuse.', 221.002, 222.844, NULL),
  (26936, 134, 'The real reason not to use drugs -
they damage your brain.', 222.845, 227.059, NULL),
  (26937, 134, 'Obsessive–compulsive disorder', 228.059, 229.753, NULL),
  (26938, 134, 'where the front part of the brain
typically works too hard,', 229.754, 232.925, NULL),
  (26939, 134, 'so that people cannot
turn off their thoughts.', 233.745, 236.736, NULL),
  (26940, 134, 'An epilepsy where we frequently
see areas of increased activity.', 237.406, 243.379, NULL),
  (26941, 134, 'In 1992, I went to an all-day conference
on brain SPECT imaging,', 244.473, 248.822, NULL),
  (26942, 134, 'it was amazing and mirrored', 248.823, 251.959, NULL),
  (26943, 134, 'our own early experience
using SPECT in psychiatry.', 251.960, 257.899, NULL),
  (26944, 134, 'But at that same meeting,
researchers started to complain loudly', 257.901, 263.202, NULL),
  (26945, 134, 'that clinical psychiatrists like me
should not be doing scans,', 263.203, 267.667, NULL),
  (26946, 134, 'that they were only for their research.', 267.668, 271.699, NULL),
  (26947, 134, 'Being the maverick
and having clinical experience,', 272.519, 277.196, NULL),
  (26948, 134, 'I thought that was a really dumb idea.', 277.197, 280.251, NULL),
  (26949, 134, '(Laughter)', 280.252, 281.527, NULL),
  (26950, 134, 'Without imaging,', 282.177, 284.198, NULL),
  (26951, 134, 'psychiatrists then and even now
make diagnosis like they did in 1840,', 284.199, 289.913, NULL),
  (26952, 134, 'when Abraham Lincoln was depressed,', 289.914, 292.800, NULL),
  (26953, 134, 'by talking to people and looking
for symptom clusters.', 292.801, 297.533, NULL),
  (26954, 134, 'Imaging was showing us
there was a better way.', 298.323, 301.630, NULL),
  (26955, 134, 'Did you know that psychiatrists
are the only medical specialists', 301.631, 306.748, NULL),
  (26956, 134, 'that virtually never look
at the organ they treat?', 306.749, 310.275, NULL),
  (26957, 134, 'Think about it!', 310.276, 311.414, NULL),
  (26958, 134, 'Cardiologists look, neurologists look,
orthopedic doctors look,', 311.894, 317.399, NULL),
  (26959, 134, 'virtually every other
medical specialties look -', 317.400, 321.665, NULL),
  (26960, 134, 'psychiatrists guess.', 321.666, 323.579, NULL),
  (26961, 134, 'Before imaging,', 324.589, 325.937, NULL),
  (26962, 134, 'I always felt like I was throwing
darts in the dark at my patients', 325.938, 331.798, NULL),
  (26963, 134, 'and had hurt some of them
which horrified me.', 331.799, 337.170, NULL),
  (26964, 134, 'There is a reason', 337.760, 339.191, NULL),
  (26965, 134, 'that most psychiatric medications
have black box warnings.', 339.192, 342.674, NULL),
  (26966, 134, 'Give them to the wrong person,
and you can precipitate a disaster.', 343.274, 349.230, NULL),
  (26967, 134, 'Early on, our imaging work
taught us many important lessons,', 351.722, 356.082, NULL),
  (26968, 134, 'such as illnesses, like ADHD,
anxiety, depression, and addictions,', 356.083, 360.166, NULL),
  (26969, 134, 'are not simple or single
disorders in the brain,', 360.183, 364.403, NULL),
  (26970, 134, 'they all have multiple types.', 364.404, 367.040, NULL),
  (26971, 134, 'For example, here are two patients', 367.041, 369.263, NULL),
  (26972, 134, 'who have been diagnosed
with major depression,', 369.264, 372.542, NULL),
  (26973, 134, 'that had virtually the same symptoms,
yet radically different brains.', 372.543, 378.105, NULL),
  (26974, 134, 'One had really low activity in the brain,
the other one had really high activity.', 378.106, 384.199, NULL),
  (26975, 134, 'How would you ever know what to do
for them, unless you actually looked?', 385.464, 391.235, NULL),
  (26976, 134, 'Treatment needs to be tailored', 391.662, 394.428, NULL),
  (26977, 134, 'to individual brains,
not clusters of symptoms.', 394.429, 399.276, NULL),
  (26978, 134, 'Our imaging work also taught us', 400.352, 402.276, NULL),
  (26979, 134, 'that mild traumatic brain injury
was a major cause of psychiatric illness', 402.277, 408.514, NULL),
  (26980, 134, 'that ruin people''s lives,', 408.515, 410.684, NULL),
  (26981, 134, 'and virtually no one knew about it
because they would see psychiatrists', 410.685, 415.713, NULL),
  (26982, 134, 'for things like temper problems,
anxiety, depression, and insomnia,', 415.714, 420.690, NULL),
  (26983, 134, 'and they would never look,
so they would never know.', 420.691, 423.918, NULL),
  (26984, 134, 'Here''s a scan of a 15-year-old boy', 424.838, 427.921, NULL),
  (26985, 134, 'who felt down a flight of stairs
at the age of three.', 427.922, 431.615, NULL),
  (26986, 134, 'Even though he was unconscious
for only a few minutes,', 432.335, 437.204, NULL),
  (26987, 134, 'there was nothing mild
about the enduring effect', 438.554, 444.543, NULL),
  (26988, 134, 'that injury had on this boy''s life.', 444.544, 447.549, NULL),
  (26989, 134, 'When I met him at the age of 15,
he had just been kicked out', 447.550, 452.123, NULL),
  (26990, 134, 'of his third residential
treatment program for violence.', 452.124, 456.525, NULL),
  (26991, 134, 'He needed a brain rehabilitation program,', 456.526, 460.077, NULL),
  (26992, 134, 'not just more medication
thrown at him in the dark,', 460.078, 465.044, NULL),
  (26993, 134, 'or behavioral therapy which,
if you think about it, is really cruel.', 465.045, 470.504, NULL),
  (26994, 134, 'To put him on a behavioral therapy program', 470.505, 472.984, NULL),
  (26995, 134, 'when behavior is really an expression
of the problem, it''s not the problem.', 472.985, 478.437, NULL),
  (26996, 134, 'Researchers have found
that undiagnosed brain injuries', 479.500, 482.921, NULL),
  (26997, 134, 'are a major cause of homelessness,
drug and alcohol abuse, depression,', 482.922, 488.130, NULL),
  (26998, 134, 'panic attacks, ADHD, and suicide.', 488.131, 491.617, NULL),
  (26999, 134, 'We are in for a pending disaster', 492.126, 495.496, NULL),
  (27000, 134, 'with the hundreds
and thousands of soldiers', 495.497, 498.156, NULL),
  (27001, 134, 'coming back from Iraq and Afganistan,', 498.157, 500.565, NULL),
  (27002, 134, 'and virtually no one is looking
at the function of their brain.', 500.566, 505.342, NULL),
  (27003, 134, 'As we continued our work with SPECT,', 506.749, 510.815, NULL),
  (27004, 134, 'the criticism grew louder,
but so did the lessons.', 510.816, 515.318, NULL),
  (27005, 134, 'Judges and defense attorneys sought
our help to understand criminal behavior.', 516.140, 520.576, NULL),
  (27006, 134, 'Today, we have scanned
over 500 convicted felons', 520.577, 523.822, NULL),
  (27007, 134, 'including 90 murderers.', 523.823, 526.415, NULL),
  (27008, 134, 'Our work taught us
that people who do bad things', 526.956, 529.750, NULL),
  (27009, 134, 'often have troubled brains.', 529.751, 532.055, NULL),
  (27010, 134, 'That was not a surprise.', 532.056, 534.133, NULL),
  (27011, 134, 'But what did surprise us', 534.134, 536.708, NULL),
  (27012, 134, 'was that many of these brains
could be rehabilitated.', 536.709, 542.293, NULL),
  (27013, 134, 'So here''s a radical idea.', 543.540, 545.544, NULL),
  (27014, 134, 'What if we evaluated
and treated troubled brains', 545.545, 548.529, NULL),
  (27015, 134, 'rather than simply warehousing them
in toxic, stressful environments?', 548.530, 553.558, NULL),
  (27016, 134, 'In my experience, we could save
tremendous amounts of money', 553.559, 559.625, NULL),
  (27017, 134, 'by making these people more functional,', 560.345, 563.299, NULL),
  (27018, 134, 'so when they left prison, they could work,', 563.300, 567.238, NULL),
  (27019, 134, 'support their families and pay taxes.', 567.239, 571.049, NULL),
  (27020, 134, 'Dostoyevsky once said:
"A society should be judged', 572.389, 575.538, NULL),
  (27021, 134, 'not by how well it treats
its outstanding citizens,', 575.539, 578.805, NULL),
  (27022, 134, 'but by how it treats its criminals."', 579.905, 582.737, NULL),
  (27023, 134, 'Instead of just crime and punishment,', 583.277, 587.481, NULL),
  (27024, 134, 'we should be thinking
about crime evaluation and treatment.', 587.482, 593.686, NULL),
  (27025, 134, '(Applause)', 593.687, 595.191, NULL),
  (27026, 134, 'So after 22 years and 83,000 scans,', 600.074, 604.528, NULL),
  (27027, 134, 'the single most important lesson
my colleagues and I have learned', 605.378, 610.077, NULL),
  (27028, 134, 'is that you can literally
change people''s brains.', 610.078, 612.495, NULL),
  (27029, 134, 'And when you do, you change their life.', 613.365, 616.242, NULL),
  (27030, 134, 'You are not stuck with the brain you have,', 616.243, 618.548, NULL),
  (27031, 134, 'you can make it better,
and we can prove it.', 618.549, 621.874, NULL),
  (27032, 134, 'My colleagues and I performed
the first and largest study', 622.524, 626.798, NULL),
  (27033, 134, 'on active and retired NFL players,', 626.799, 629.881, NULL),
  (27034, 134, 'showing high levels of damage
in these players at the time', 629.882, 634.275, NULL),
  (27035, 134, 'when the NFL said they didn''t know', 634.276, 638.045, NULL),
  (27036, 134, 'if playing football caused
long-term brain damage.', 638.046, 640.742, NULL),
  (27037, 134, 'The fact was they didn''t want to know.', 641.562, 644.106, NULL),
  (27038, 134, 'That was not a surprise.', 644.107, 645.327, NULL),
  (27039, 134, 'I think, if you get the most thoughtful
9-year-olds together,', 645.334, 648.210, NULL),
  (27040, 134, 'and you talk about the brain is soft,
about the consistency of soft butter,', 648.217, 652.334, NULL),
  (27041, 134, 'it''s housed in a really hard skull
that has many sharp, bony ridges,', 652.335, 656.423, NULL),
  (27042, 134, 'you know, 28 out of 30
nine-year-olds would go:', 656.424, 659.765, NULL),
  (27043, 134, '"Probably a bad idea for your life."', 659.766, 662.259, NULL),
  (27044, 134, '(Laughter)', 662.260, 663.932, NULL),
  (27045, 134, 'But what really got us excited
was the second part of the study', 664.812, 669.801, NULL),
  (27046, 134, 'where we put players
on a brain-smart program', 669.802, 674.736, NULL),
  (27047, 134, 'and demonstrated
that 80% of them could improve', 674.737, 680.019, NULL),
  (27048, 134, 'in the areas of blood flow,
memory, and mood,', 680.020, 683.845, NULL),
  (27049, 134, 'that you are not stuck
with the brain you have,', 683.846, 687.148, NULL),
  (27050, 134, 'you can make it better
on a brain-smart program.', 687.149, 691.329, NULL),
  (27051, 134, 'How exciting is that?', 691.330, 693.038, NULL),
  (27052, 134, 'I am so excited.', 693.039, 694.829, NULL),
  (27053, 134, 'Reversing brain damage
is a very exciting new frontier,', 694.834, 699.126, NULL),
  (27054, 134, 'but the implications
are really much wider.', 699.127, 702.709, NULL),
  (27055, 134, 'Here is this scan
of a teenage girl who has ADHD,', 702.710, 707.163, NULL),
  (27056, 134, 'who was cutting herself, failing
in school, and fighting with her parents.', 707.164, 712.240, NULL),
  (27057, 134, 'When we improved her brain,', 712.880, 715.306, NULL),
  (27058, 134, 'she went from D''s and F''s to A''s and B''s,', 715.307, 720.096, NULL),
  (27059, 134, 'and was much more emotionally stable.', 720.097, 722.799, NULL),
  (27060, 134, 'Here is the scan of Nancy.', 723.389, 725.485, NULL),
  (27061, 134, 'Nancy had been diagnosed with dementia,', 725.486, 728.693, NULL),
  (27062, 134, 'and her doctor told her husband
that he should find a home for her', 728.694, 733.332, NULL),
  (27063, 134, 'because within a year,
she would not know his name.', 733.333, 737.517, NULL),
  (27064, 134, 'But on an intensive,
brain-rehabilitation program,', 738.377, 744.984, NULL),
  (27065, 134, 'Nancy''s brain was better,
as was her memory,', 745.814, 750.407, NULL),
  (27066, 134, 'and four years later,
Nancy still knows her husband''s name.', 750.408, 755.987, NULL),
  (27067, 134, 'Or my favorite story
to illustrate this point: Andrew,', 756.969, 761.253, NULL),
  (27068, 134, 'a 9-year-old boy who attacked
a little girl on the baseball field', 761.253, 765.160, NULL),
  (27069, 134, 'for no particular reason,', 765.161, 767.399, NULL),
  (27070, 134, 'and at the time,
was drawing pictures of himself', 767.400, 770.758, NULL),
  (27071, 134, 'hanging from a tree
and shooting other children.', 770.759, 775.041, NULL),
  (27072, 134, 'Andrew was Columbine, Aurora,', 776.308, 780.204, NULL),
  (27073, 134, 'and Sandy Hook waiting to happen.', 781.664, 784.490, NULL),
  (27074, 134, 'Most psychiatrists
would have medicated Andrew,', 784.491, 786.956, NULL),
  (27075, 134, 'as they did Eric Harris
and the other mass shooters', 786.957, 791.491, NULL),
  (27076, 134, 'before they committed their awful crimes,', 791.492, 794.355, NULL),
  (27077, 134, 'but SPECT imaging taught me
that I had to look at his brain', 794.356, 799.060, NULL),
  (27078, 134, 'and not throw darts in the dark at him
to understand what he needed.', 799.061, 803.885, NULL),
  (27079, 134, 'His SPECT scan showed
a cyst, the size of a golf ball,', 804.465, 810.209, NULL),
  (27080, 134, 'occupying the space
of his left temple lobe.', 810.210, 814.005, NULL),
  (27081, 134, 'No amount of medication or therapy
would have helped Andrew.', 814.006, 817.737, NULL),
  (27082, 134, 'When the cyst was removed,', 817.738, 820.075, NULL),
  (27083, 134, 'his behavior completely
went back to normal,', 821.685, 825.150, NULL),
  (27084, 134, 'and he became the sweet, loving boy
he always wanted to be.', 825.151, 830.863, NULL),
  (27085, 134, 'Now 18 years later,
Andrew, who is my nephew,', 831.738, 835.510, NULL),
  (27086, 134, 'owns his own home,
is employed and pays taxes.', 836.520, 841.237, NULL),
  (27087, 134, '(Laughter)', 841.238, 843.309, NULL),
  (27088, 134, 'Because someone bothered
to look at his brain,', 843.310, 847.418, NULL),
  (27089, 134, 'he has been a better son,', 847.419, 850.530, NULL),
  (27090, 134, 'and will be a better husband,
father, and grandfather.', 850.531, 856.480, NULL),
  (27091, 134, 'When you have the privilege
of changing someone''s brain,', 857.781, 862.563, NULL),
  (27092, 134, 'you not only change his or her life', 862.564, 865.660, NULL),
  (27093, 134, 'but you have the opportunity
to change generations to come.', 865.661, 870.745, NULL),
  (27094, 134, 'I''m Dr. Daniel Amen. Thank you.', 871.627, 873.569, NULL),
  (27095, 134, '(Applause)', 873.570, 875.255, NULL),
  (27096, 135, 'Reviewer: Zsuzsa Viola', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (27097, 135, 'Namaste!', 9.116, 10.147, NULL),
  (27098, 135, 'Today, as you see me
as a package of success,', 10.147, 12.559, NULL),
  (27099, 135, 'when my bio says that I have cleared
all the top prestigious exams', 12.559, 16.979, NULL),
  (27100, 135, 'and interviews of India.', 16.979, 18.699, NULL),
  (27101, 135, 'My friends, let me tell you
not more about my successes', 19.518, 23.364, NULL),
  (27102, 135, 'but more about my rejections, my failures,
and my determination, my willpower', 23.364, 28.919, NULL),
  (27103, 135, 'that made me get those successes.', 28.919, 31.180, NULL),
  (27104, 135, 'So my story starts from a small
sleepy village of Madhya Pradesh', 31.539, 36.390, NULL),
  (27105, 135, 'with a population
of barely a thousand people.', 36.580, 39.880, NULL),
  (27106, 135, 'On the month of a rainy August,', 39.880, 42.489, NULL),
  (27107, 135, 'a small girl was born
in an orthodox Brahmin family -', 42.489, 46.890, NULL),
  (27108, 135, 'a family that was giant
and joint with 30 plus members -', 46.890, 50.971, NULL),
  (27109, 135, 'it was not an event for them.', 51.311, 53.702, NULL),
  (27110, 135, 'There was nothing that worth celebrating
happened that day when I was born,', 53.702, 57.242, NULL),
  (27111, 135, 'only two souls on Earth were happy,', 57.242, 59.382, NULL),
  (27112, 135, 'obviously, they were my parents,', 59.382, 61.592, NULL),
  (27113, 135, 'for the rest of them,
it was a normal affair.', 61.592, 64.243, NULL),
  (27114, 135, '25 years down the line,
same girl, same village,', 65.093, 69.963, NULL),
  (27115, 135, 'and the whole family
was welcoming her with garlands,', 70.196, 73.063, NULL),
  (27116, 135, 'bang bang slogans like,', 73.063, 74.624, NULL),
  (27117, 135, '(Hindi) "What should a girl look like?
Like Surabhi Gautam! Why not?"', 74.624, 78.094, NULL),
  (27118, 135, 'What made things
to become so different for her?', 78.094, 81.184, NULL),
  (27119, 135, '(Applause)', 81.184, 83.164, NULL),
  (27120, 135, 'My dear friends, let me tell you
how things changed', 84.692, 87.538, NULL),
  (27121, 135, 'not only for me but also for my parents,', 87.538, 90.193, NULL),
  (27122, 135, 'how all the perspectives got changed
slowly, slowly, steadily, steadily.', 90.193, 94.724, NULL),
  (27123, 135, 'I was in a joint family.', 95.924, 97.244, NULL),
  (27124, 135, 'In a joint family, you know,
no child gets separate attention.', 97.244, 102.745, NULL),
  (27125, 135, 'So we all were treated equally.', 102.745, 104.235, NULL),
  (27126, 135, 'Life was OK. We were happy.', 104.235, 106.625, NULL),
  (27127, 135, 'I got admission in my village school.', 106.625, 109.259, NULL),
  (27128, 135, 'That was Hindi medium:', 109.259, 110.685, NULL),
  (27129, 135, 'Madhya Pradesh Board School.', 110.685, 112.708, NULL),
  (27130, 135, 'In 5th class,', 113.946, 115.176, NULL),
  (27131, 135, 'something good happened with me
that I remember till date.', 115.176, 119.246, NULL),
  (27132, 135, 'I got 100 out of 100
in my mathematics paper.', 119.246, 122.877, NULL),
  (27133, 135, '5th class was a board class.', 122.877, 124.741, NULL),
  (27134, 135, 'So my teacher called me, and she said,', 125.257, 127.687, NULL),
  (27135, 135, '"See, I have never seen anybody
scoring full marks,', 127.687, 130.167, NULL),
  (27136, 135, 'that in mathematics, that in board exam.', 130.167, 132.828, NULL),
  (27137, 135, 'You have done this,', 132.828, 133.837, NULL),
  (27138, 135, 'so I think you are going to do
something good in your studies."', 133.837, 137.439, NULL),
  (27139, 135, 'That was the day', 137.868, 138.943, NULL),
  (27140, 135, 'when I felt appreciated and recognized,', 138.943, 141.388, NULL),
  (27141, 135, 'and I had given this
clear message to the Universe', 141.388, 144.641, NULL),
  (27142, 135, 'that in future, all I''m going to do
is to be a studious girl', 144.641, 148.028, NULL),
  (27143, 135, 'because with studies comes recognition,', 148.028, 150.589, NULL),
  (27144, 135, 'with studies will come
appreciation for me.', 150.589, 153.249, NULL),
  (27145, 135, 'Otherwise, in this family,
I''m not going to get this at all.', 153.249, 156.579, NULL),
  (27146, 135, 'So I started to focus more on studies.', 156.579, 160.099, NULL),
  (27147, 135, 'But my heart - it always
wanted to diversify.', 160.330, 163.170, NULL),
  (27148, 135, 'I wanted to do everything.', 163.170, 164.500, NULL),
  (27149, 135, 'I started to try my hand
at painting, sketching, drawing.', 164.500, 168.471, NULL),
  (27150, 135, 'I started to do embroidery also.', 168.471, 170.561, NULL),
  (27151, 135, 'I was busy with my village priest,', 170.561, 173.316, NULL),
  (27152, 135, 'and all the pujas,', 173.316, 174.671, NULL),
  (27153, 135, 'and on all the Ramayan
(Hindi) events (English) and everything.', 174.671, 177.631, NULL),
  (27154, 135, 'And I was not noticing the pain
that was creeping in my body.', 177.631, 181.614, NULL),
  (27155, 135, 'I started to feel the pain
in my joints and my elbow', 181.782, 185.142, NULL),
  (27156, 135, 'and every joint of my body,', 185.142, 187.049, NULL),
  (27157, 135, 'and after some time, I was bedridden.', 187.049, 189.472, NULL),
  (27158, 135, 'My parents took this decision
with their meager resources', 189.983, 193.223, NULL),
  (27159, 135, 'to take me there.', 193.223, 194.733, NULL),
  (27160, 135, 'We went there to a place called Jabalpur.', 194.733, 197.384, NULL),
  (27161, 135, 'And the doctor said, "Your daughter
has this rheumatic fever."', 197.384, 202.005, NULL),
  (27162, 135, 'What happens in this disease is -', 202.580, 204.664, NULL),
  (27163, 135, 'there are viruses
always present in the air.', 204.764, 207.794, NULL),
  (27164, 135, 'Now and then, they attack
the body of children,', 207.794, 210.195, NULL),
  (27165, 135, 'and they create pain.', 210.195, 211.435, NULL),
  (27166, 135, 'And when it becomes serious,
what happens, they attack your heart', 211.435, 215.235, NULL),
  (27167, 135, 'and they disturb the semilunar valve.', 215.235, 218.209, NULL),
  (27168, 135, 'And in some cases, it leads to death also.', 218.635, 221.716, NULL),
  (27169, 135, 'It was a shock for them.', 222.316, 224.093, NULL),
  (27170, 135, 'But then they asked,
"What can be the possible treatment?"', 225.116, 228.766, NULL),
  (27171, 135, 'As a treatment, the doctor suggested', 229.547, 231.747, NULL),
  (27172, 135, 'that she should be given
the dose of antibiotic,', 231.747, 235.638, NULL),
  (27173, 135, 'and that antibiotic was penicillin.', 235.923, 238.319, NULL),
  (27174, 135, 'There is some problem
with penicillin. What happens?', 238.387, 241.177, NULL),
  (27175, 135, 'As soon as it enters the body,
it gets solidified', 241.177, 244.307, NULL),
  (27176, 135, 'when it comes in contact with air.', 244.307, 246.128, NULL),
  (27177, 135, 'So it was again a problem', 246.128, 247.438, NULL),
  (27178, 135, 'because I had to be injected
with penicillin in every 15 days.', 247.438, 251.622, NULL),
  (27179, 135, 'And not every MBBS doctor
was ready to do this', 251.752, 254.912, NULL),
  (27180, 135, 'because it can also
lead to death in some cases.', 255.167, 258.687, NULL),
  (27181, 135, 'So in the village, in every 15 days,', 259.331, 261.642, NULL),
  (27182, 135, 'it was also difficult
to get a skilled doctor', 261.720, 265.170, NULL),
  (27183, 135, 'to inject me with the confidence
that I will not die.', 265.170, 268.120, NULL),
  (27184, 135, 'Well, life was going OK, OK.', 269.790, 272.909, NULL),
  (27185, 135, 'There was a problem
of electricity in my village.', 272.909, 275.201, NULL),
  (27186, 135, 'So I had to study by the kerosene lamp.', 275.201, 277.970, NULL),
  (27187, 135, 'I had other problems.', 277.970, 279.080, NULL),
  (27188, 135, 'There was no tuition.', 279.080, 280.221, NULL),
  (27189, 135, 'School situation was also very bad.', 280.221, 282.769, NULL),
  (27190, 135, 'Then the second best thing
of my life happened.', 283.732, 286.252, NULL),
  (27191, 135, 'It was the 10th class result.', 287.062, 289.072, NULL),
  (27192, 135, 'My 10th results came,', 289.072, 290.512, NULL),
  (27193, 135, 'and I again scored 100 out of 100 -', 290.512, 292.502, NULL),
  (27194, 135, 'this time not only in mathematics
but also in science.', 292.502, 296.473, NULL),
  (27195, 135, '(Applause)', 296.473, 298.033, NULL),
  (27196, 135, 'And my percentage was good enough
to place me on the state merit list.', 298.033, 304.214, NULL),
  (27197, 135, 'Well, I became', 304.214, 305.219, NULL),
  (27198, 135, 'a pseudo-celebrity of my village.', 305.219, 306.864, NULL),
  (27199, 135, 'I was in the news for quite a week,
and the newspaper interviewer came to me,', 307.334, 311.454, NULL),
  (27200, 135, 'and he started to ask me questions,', 311.614, 313.584, NULL),
  (27201, 135, '"How did you do this?" you know?', 313.584, 315.154, NULL),
  (27202, 135, '"This is a great achievement and all."', 315.154, 317.335, NULL),
  (27203, 135, 'And at last, he asked one question,', 317.335, 319.384, NULL),
  (27204, 135, '"Surabhi, what do you want
to become when you grow up?', 319.384, 321.915, NULL),
