  (27453, 135, 'because for others,
you have already proved.', 980.414, 982.502, NULL),
  (27454, 135, 'This is your task. You have to do.', 982.502, 984.172, NULL),
  (27455, 135, 'And you are saying
life is difficult for you.', 984.172, 986.453, NULL),
  (27456, 135, 'You need to change your lenses better."', 986.453, 989.063, NULL),
  (27457, 135, 'That day I stopped complaining
mostly, at least with her,', 989.063, 992.953, NULL),
  (27458, 135, 'and I was totally on a mission mode.', 992.953, 995.933, NULL),
  (27459, 135, 'All my scarcities,
I converted them into my luxuries.', 996.243, 1000.124, NULL),
  (27460, 135, 'The more I struggled,
the more strong I became.', 1000.514, 1003.294, NULL),
  (27461, 135, 'And finally, I got All India Rank 50
in this coveted exam -', 1003.294, 1007.825, NULL),
  (27462, 135, 'Civil Services Examination 2016.', 1007.825, 1009.875, NULL),
  (27463, 135, '(Applause)', 1009.875, 1012.465, NULL),
  (27464, 135, 'To summarize:', 1012.465, 1013.765, NULL),
  (27465, 135, 'At last, I believed in these words.', 1013.765, 1016.445, NULL),
  (27466, 135, 'These words truly tell my story.', 1016.445, 1018.655, NULL),
  (27467, 135, 'And I also want to convey
these words to you also,', 1019.015, 1021.974, NULL),
  (27468, 135, '"There is no substitute for hard work,
and there is no shortcut to success."', 1022.584, 1027.395, NULL),
  (27469, 135, 'And my own four lines that I wrote -', 1028.547, 1030.947, NULL),
  (27470, 135, 'I want to say (Hindi),', 1030.947, 1032.838, NULL),
  (27471, 135, '"Had I mourned for what I had not got -
Had I mourned for what I had not got', 1032.838, 1038.278, NULL),
  (27472, 135, 'I wouldn''t have been able
to improve in the opportunities I got.', 1038.599, 1041.658, NULL),
  (27473, 135, 'It is stubbornness to fight
with fate and achieve something.', 1041.658, 1046.567, NULL),
  (27474, 135, 'These things would not
have arisen in me like this.', 1046.567, 1048.949, NULL),
  (27475, 135, 'But it was my promise
to myself to keep on moving', 1048.949, 1051.280, NULL),
  (27476, 135, 'I also mourned about getting nothing.', 1051.280, 1053.510, NULL),
  (27477, 135, 'But it was my promise
to myself to keep on moving.', 1054.009, 1058.680, NULL),
  (27478, 135, 'Whatever my steps measured is less.', 1058.680, 1061.540, NULL),
  (27479, 135, 'Whatever my steps measured is less.', 1061.680, 1064.640, NULL),
  (27480, 135, 'This is the secret
to reach your destination.', 1064.640, 1066.760, NULL),
  (27481, 135, 'This is the secret
to reach your destination."', 1066.810, 1068.950, NULL),
  (27482, 135, '(Applause)', 1068.950, 1071.950, NULL),
  (27483, 135, 'Thanks for being such a patient
and such a good audience.', 1075.946, 1079.347, NULL),
  (27484, 135, 'Thanks TED and thanks to everyone.', 1079.347, 1081.742, NULL),
  (27485, 135, '(Applause) (Cheering)', 1081.742, 1084.782, NULL),
  (27486, 136, 'Transcriber: Yunhan Jiang
Reviewer: Rhonda Jacobs', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (27487, 136, 'Good morning.', 24.016, 25.622, NULL),
  (27488, 136, '(Ethereal music)', 25.622, 27.226, NULL),
  (27489, 136, 'It has been quite a privilege', 27.226, 30.154, NULL),
  (27490, 136, 'being able to grow up
in two quite different ways of life.', 30.154, 36.533, NULL),
  (27491, 136, 'I was born in Germany,', 38.161, 40.443, NULL),
  (27492, 136, 'and at the same time had the chance', 40.443, 43.865, NULL),
  (27493, 136, 'to learn more about an ancient art
coming from the Shaolin Temple.', 43.865, 48.903, NULL),
  (27494, 136, 'When you grow up in an Asian family,', 49.333, 51.711, NULL),
  (27495, 136, 'it is quite common', 51.711, 53.489, NULL),
  (27496, 136, 'that firstly, you don''t argue
with your father,', 53.489, 57.911, NULL),
  (27497, 136, 'and secondly, you either
become medical doctor,', 58.551, 63.312, NULL),
  (27498, 136, 'engineer, or lawyer.', 63.622, 66.309, NULL),
  (27499, 136, 'Elsewise your parents
will be very unhappy.', 66.309, 71.530, NULL),
  (27500, 136, 'So having that said,', 72.000, 75.768, NULL),
  (27501, 136, 'I finished my academic education
with two university degrees,', 76.247, 81.830, NULL),
  (27502, 136, 'an MBA,', 81.830, 83.390, NULL),
  (27503, 136, 'and quite a collection
of different certificates and diplomas -', 84.280, 89.388, NULL),
  (27504, 136, 'everything that my parents thought
would be useful to have.', 89.388, 94.734, NULL),
  (27505, 136, 'But throughout this education,', 95.074, 98.601, NULL),
  (27506, 136, 'I felt something was missing.', 100.506, 102.687, NULL),
  (27507, 136, 'Because I was learning
about many different aspects -', 104.266, 109.789, NULL),
  (27508, 136, 'how the plant is working,', 110.519, 112.682, NULL),
  (27509, 136, 'what an atom is made out of,', 113.121, 115.628, NULL),
  (27510, 136, 'how a political system is functioning,', 116.211, 119.123, NULL),
  (27511, 136, 'but somehow, the subject was missing', 120.063, 123.657, NULL),
  (27512, 136, 'to learn something about myself.', 124.341, 127.915, NULL),
  (27513, 136, 'So with the age of four,', 129.941, 132.127, NULL),
  (27514, 136, 'for the first time', 132.127, 133.441, NULL),
  (27515, 136, 'I got introduced
into the monastic practices,', 133.441, 137.647, NULL),
  (27516, 136, 'and I was very happy to find out
that the main part of these practices', 138.927, 145.060, NULL),
  (27517, 136, 'were dealing with the exploration
and the discovery of yourself.', 145.060, 151.009, NULL),
  (27518, 136, 'There was mental training,', 153.222, 155.284, NULL),
  (27519, 136, 'development of behavior
combined with the physical training,', 156.926, 163.183, NULL),
  (27520, 136, 'all aspects of what nowadays 
is known as Shaolin Kung-Fu.', 163.183, 168.546, NULL),
  (27521, 136, 'Now, despite the wishes of my parents', 170.716, 172.786, NULL),
  (27522, 136, 'to somehow go out in the market
and try to manage the world,', 172.786, 178.853, NULL),
  (27523, 136, 'I decided to continue this monastic life', 180.299, 185.699, NULL),
  (27524, 136, 'and start learning more
about myself first.', 186.768, 192.006, NULL),
  (27525, 136, 'Now, in the preparation for this talk,', 193.487, 197.237, NULL),
  (27526, 136, 'I was asked to share a few words on', 197.237, 202.358, NULL),
  (27527, 136, 'what is important in this lifetime,', 203.479, 206.424, NULL),
  (27528, 136, 'and see,', 207.998, 209.387, NULL),
  (27529, 136, 'it''s already challenging', 211.719, 214.719, NULL),
  (27530, 136, 'to put three decades into a single talk.', 215.957, 219.691, NULL),
  (27531, 136, 'But the picture I would like to show you', 221.544, 225.684, NULL),
  (27532, 136, 'summarizes very much', 226.531, 228.971, NULL),
  (27533, 136, 'what I consider
as being valuable in this lifetime.', 230.605, 235.254, NULL),
  (27534, 136, 'There is something
about sharing with others.', 237.408, 242.626, NULL),
  (27535, 136, 'There is something about connection.', 244.452, 246.922, NULL),
  (27536, 136, 'There is the training
and development of yourself.', 247.172, 251.261, NULL),
  (27537, 136, 'It is to enjoy your time,
even doing nothing.', 251.261, 255.681, NULL),
  (27538, 136, 'And one main aspect is', 256.093, 258.790, NULL),
  (27539, 136, 'to find a way', 260.000, 261.474, NULL),
  (27540, 136, 'and do the things you like to do.', 262.177, 265.547, NULL),
  (27541, 136, 'Now, when I received the invitation', 266.779, 270.499, NULL),
  (27542, 136, 'to have a talk at today''s event,', 270.869, 273.045, NULL),
  (27543, 136, 'especially under the slogan
"High, Higher, Highest,"', 273.045, 277.329, NULL),
  (27544, 136, 'something very particular
came up on my mind,', 278.087, 282.972, NULL),
  (27545, 136, 'and a master from the Shaolin Temple', 283.352, 288.449, NULL),
  (27546, 136, 'once told me a story
that I would like to share with you.', 289.219, 295.325, NULL),
  (27547, 136, '(Flute music)', 296.341, 298.716, NULL),
  (27548, 136, 'A man was living close to a mountain,', 300.787, 303.196, NULL),
  (27549, 136, 'and every day he was thinking:', 303.766, 306.522, NULL),
  (27550, 136, 'How would it be to climb that mountain', 307.226, 311.006, NULL),
  (27551, 136, 'and what would I see on the peak?', 311.006, 313.526, NULL),
  (27552, 136, 'So finally, the day came, 
and the man went on the journey.', 314.096, 320.464, NULL),
  (27553, 136, 'Arriving at the foot of the mountain,', 321.514, 324.019, NULL),
  (27554, 136, 'he met the first traveler.', 324.019, 326.037, NULL),
  (27555, 136, 'So he asked,', 327.029, 328.459, NULL),
  (27556, 136, '"How did you get up the mountain,
and what did you see from the top?"', 329.169, 333.939, NULL),
  (27557, 136, 'And so the traveler shared his path,', 334.199, 336.299, NULL),
  (27558, 136, 'and also the view that he had.', 336.299, 338.749, NULL),
  (27559, 136, 'But then the man was thinking,', 340.053, 342.363, NULL),
  (27560, 136, '"The way that this traveler described
to me sounds very exhausting.', 344.113, 349.178, NULL),
  (27561, 136, 'I need to find another way to climb."', 350.158, 352.713, NULL),
  (27562, 136, 'So he continued to walk
on the foot of the mountain', 353.751, 356.623, NULL),
  (27563, 136, 'until he met the next traveler.', 356.623, 359.116, NULL),
  (27564, 136, 'So once again he asked,', 359.366, 361.504, NULL),
  (27565, 136, '"How did you climb up that mountain,', 362.244, 364.747, NULL),
  (27566, 136, 'and what did you see from the top?"', 365.087, 367.520, NULL),
  (27567, 136, 'And so again the traveler
shared his story.', 368.760, 371.550, NULL),
  (27568, 136, 'Still not being determined
on which direction and which way to go,', 373.971, 378.230, NULL),
  (27569, 136, 'the man asked 30 more people,
30 more travelers.', 380.110, 384.910, NULL),
  (27570, 136, 'When he finished talking to all of them,', 385.610, 388.200, NULL),
  (27571, 136, 'he finally made up his mind.', 388.200, 390.578, NULL),
  (27572, 136, '"Now that so many people
already shared with me their paths', 391.120, 394.650, NULL),
  (27573, 136, 'and especially what
they all saw from the top,', 394.650, 398.730, NULL),
  (27574, 136, 'I don''t need to climb there anymore."', 398.730, 401.311, NULL),
  (27575, 136, 'It is very unfortunate', 401.950, 403.990, NULL),
  (27576, 136, 'this man never went on the journey.', 404.400, 407.494, NULL),
  (27577, 136, 'Now, to conclude this story,', 409.127, 411.705, NULL),
  (27578, 136, 'firstly,', 413.257, 414.492, NULL),
  (27579, 136, 'each individual needs to find
the most suitable way', 415.862, 421.500, NULL),
  (27580, 136, 'to climb that mountain.', 421.500, 423.777, NULL),
  (27581, 136, 'But secondly, there is information', 425.754, 429.841, NULL),
  (27582, 136, 'possible to be shared with words,', 430.500, 433.537, NULL),
  (27583, 136, 'but it is impossible', 434.884, 437.289, NULL),
  (27584, 136, 'to share the experience of clarity', 438.993, 442.819, NULL),
  (27585, 136, 'when you are standing
on that peak by yourself.', 442.819, 447.409, NULL),
  (27586, 136, 'To invest the right effort', 449.138, 453.872, NULL),
  (27587, 136, 'in climbing that peak,', 454.562, 457.069, NULL),
  (27588, 136, 'it''s very much what
all the Buddhist practices,', 458.037, 463.966, NULL),
  (27589, 136, 'the Shaolin training,', 464.637, 466.304, NULL),
  (27590, 136, 'or any spiritual practice is about.', 467.784, 471.148, NULL),
  (27591, 136, 'Clarity means you see more clear.', 472.922, 477.357, NULL),
  (27592, 136, 'When you see more clear,
interrelations become more apparent.', 477.687, 483.497, NULL),
  (27593, 136, 'When you see more clear,', 483.757, 485.187, NULL),
  (27594, 136, 'there is no need to believe anyone
or believe anything.', 485.187, 492.117, NULL),
  (27595, 136, 'Seeing clear means 
you can distinguish for yourself', 493.165, 497.494, NULL),
  (27596, 136, 'which is the proper direction to take', 497.494, 500.720, NULL),
  (27597, 136, 'and which decisions do I have to make', 501.090, 505.362, NULL),
  (27598, 136, 'in order to make my goals
or aspirations start to shape?', 505.362, 511.923, NULL),
  (27599, 136, 'Now, at today''s talk,
you will have the chance', 512.203, 515.653, NULL),
  (27600, 136, 'to become inspired 
by quite a lot of different travelers.', 515.653, 521.039, NULL),
  (27601, 136, 'But in this particular talk,', 521.279, 523.844, NULL),
  (27602, 136, 'I can''t, and I won''t tell you
which way to go.', 524.579, 528.840, NULL),
  (27603, 136, 'It''s just that along
your personal journey,', 530.601, 536.768, NULL),
  (27604, 136, 'you will encounter challenges.', 538.704, 541.849, NULL),
  (27605, 136, 'Those challenges will either prevent you,', 542.979, 546.799, NULL),
  (27606, 136, 'or some of them even stop you,', 547.139, 549.898, NULL),
  (27607, 136, 'from moving on and climbing that mountain.', 550.378, 553.632, NULL),
  (27608, 136, 'In the Shaolin Temple,
we refer to them', 555.004, 558.764, NULL),
  (27609, 136, 'as "the five hindrances."', 559.224, 563.630, NULL),
  (27610, 136, 'The five hindrances are describing
different states of the mind.', 564.680, 571.220, NULL),
  (27611, 136, 'In those states of the mind,', 572.605, 574.635, NULL),
  (27612, 136, 'it becomes very hard to see clearly', 574.635, 578.460, NULL),
  (27613, 136, 'and therefore engage
in the right decisions.', 578.460, 582.488, NULL),
  (27614, 136, 'The first hindrance
is called "sensual desire."', 582.488, 586.998, NULL),
  (27615, 136, 'Sensual desire arises in the moment', 586.998, 591.170, NULL),
  (27616, 136, 'when you are paying
attention to something', 591.170, 594.300, NULL),
  (27617, 136, 'that is giving you a positive emotion.', 594.300, 597.840, NULL),
  (27618, 136, 'This positive emotion can originate
from five gates of your body:', 598.983, 604.633, NULL),
  (27619, 136, 'Seeing, hearing, smelling,
tasting, or feeling.', 605.693, 611.750, NULL),
  (27620, 136, 'So in your mind,
you climb up that mountain.', 613.117, 618.159, NULL),
  (27621, 136, 'After one mile of walking,', 619.631, 622.011, NULL),
  (27622, 136, 'you discover a beautiful restaurant', 622.301, 625.543, NULL),
  (27623, 136, 'surrounded by beautiful people.', 626.913, 630.033, NULL),
  (27624, 136, 'You smell delicious food
and the great variety of beverages.', 630.793, 636.423, NULL),
  (27625, 136, 'When you follow that temptation,', 636.423, 639.103, NULL),
  (27626, 136, 'you have already lost your track.', 640.283, 643.463, NULL),
  (27627, 136, 'When this temptation becomes so strong', 644.153, 648.379, NULL),
  (27628, 136, 'that you don''t want
to leave that place anymore,', 648.659, 652.170, NULL),
  (27629, 136, 'then the sensual desire
has turned into an obsession.', 653.300, 657.820, NULL),
  (27630, 136, 'In both cases,', 659.738, 661.466, NULL),
  (27631, 136, 'remaining at that place means
that you can''t get clarity.', 661.776, 667.721, NULL),
  (27632, 136, 'The second hindrance, "ill-will,"', 668.201, 672.021, NULL),
  (27633, 136, 'describes the state of the mind', 672.271, 674.835, NULL),
  (27634, 136, 'that arises from negative emotions.', 675.215, 678.645, NULL),
  (27635, 136, 'In that state of the mind,', 679.425, 681.775, NULL),
  (27636, 136, 'you have an aversion,
a rejection, or simply a dislike', 681.775, 688.270, NULL),
  (27637, 136, 'against either an object, a situation,
or can be even a person.', 688.270, 694.954, NULL),
  (27638, 136, 'To simplify, it means:', 696.608, 698.741, NULL),
  (27639, 136, 'You are climbing the mountain,', 699.371, 701.761, NULL),
  (27640, 136, 'and it starts to rain,', 701.761, 704.051, NULL),
  (27641, 136, 'but you don''t like rain.', 704.341, 706.307, NULL),
  (27642, 136, 'You discover the roads are bumpy,', 707.067, 710.268, NULL),
  (27643, 136, 'but you don''t like bumpy roads.', 710.268, 712.816, NULL),
  (27644, 136, 'In order to cross the river,
you need to swim,', 713.666, 717.266, NULL),
  (27645, 136, 'but you don’t like swimming.', 717.266, 719.670, NULL),
  (27646, 136, 'Whatever it is that you dislike,', 720.376, 723.420, NULL),
  (27647, 136, 'it won’t make it a pleasant journey', 723.420, 726.188, NULL),
  (27648, 136, 'unless you learn
to let go of this ill-will.', 727.671, 731.301, NULL),
  (27649, 136, 'It’s more likely even
that you won''t continue that journey.', 731.301, 735.938, NULL),
  (27650, 136, 'The third hindrance originally
translated as "sloth and torpor."', 736.468, 740.908, NULL),
  (27651, 136, '"Sloth" means it’s
the heaviness of the body.', 740.908, 743.908, NULL),
  (27652, 136, '"Torpor" means it’s
the dullness of the mind.', 743.908, 747.719, NULL),
  (27653, 136, 'It is characterized by sleepiness,', 747.929, 751.158, NULL),
  (27654, 136, 'non-motivation,', 751.748, 753.678, NULL),
  (27655, 136, 'lack of energy,', 754.158, 755.980, NULL),
  (27656, 136, 'and oftentimes can manifest itself', 756.168, 760.014, NULL),
  (27657, 136, 'in a state of depression.', 760.014, 764.448, NULL),
  (27658, 136, 'Now, a simile used in Buddhism
describes it as "imprisonment."', 764.738, 771.323, NULL),
  (27659, 136, 'You find yourself locked in a cell.', 771.323, 774.573, NULL),
  (27660, 136, 'It becomes very hard', 775.223, 776.998, NULL),
  (27661, 136, 'to make any type
of mental or physical effort.', 776.998, 781.774, NULL),
  (27662, 136, 'So in order to continue your path,', 781.774, 784.884, NULL),
  (27663, 136, 'there is only one option left.', 784.884, 787.504, NULL),
  (27664, 136, 'You need to find a way to get out
from that hole, from that cell.', 787.504, 792.634, NULL),
  (27665, 136, 'Now, the fourth hindrance
is called "restlessness."', 792.894, 798.674, NULL),
  (27666, 136, 'It is the state of an unsettled mind.', 798.964, 802.939, NULL),
  (27667, 136, '"Unsettle mind" means
your mind cannot settle.', 803.179, 806.629, NULL),
  (27668, 136, '(Laughter)
Settle where?', 806.929, 808.819, NULL),
  (27669, 136, 'Settle in the present moment.', 809.049, 811.239, NULL),
  (27670, 136, 'An unsettled mind
either is worrying about the future', 811.469, 816.950, NULL),
  (27671, 136, 'or traveling into the past', 817.339, 819.769, NULL),
  (27672, 136, 'and rejecting,', 819.769, 822.295, NULL),
  (27673, 136, 'judging about an event
that happened into your past.', 823.345, 827.985, NULL),
  (27674, 136, 'A simile used here is the monkey mind,', 828.255, 832.072, NULL),
  (27675, 136, 'constantly jumping
from one branch to another,', 832.482, 835.805, NULL),
  (27676, 136, 'unable to stay for too long time
at the present moment.', 835.805, 840.768, NULL),
  (27677, 136, 'The problem is there is no time
to see clearly anymore.', 842.308, 848.130, NULL),
  (27678, 136, 'Now, the last of the five hindrances
is called "skeptical doubt,"', 849.374, 853.374, NULL),
  (27679, 136, 'and it''s very closely related
to a state of mind', 853.374, 858.128, NULL),
  (27680, 136, 'which is based on indecisiveness.', 858.128, 861.490, NULL),
  (27681, 136, 'It is very easy in that state of mind
getting lost in thoughts.', 861.940, 866.816, NULL),
  (27682, 136, 'Can I do this?', 867.036, 868.823, NULL),
  (27683, 136, 'Is this the right path?', 869.400, 872.034, NULL),
  (27684, 136, 'What will the others say?', 872.034, 874.009, NULL),
  (27685, 136, 'What if this? What if that?', 874.009, 876.171, NULL),
  (27686, 136, 'The mind cannot synchronize
with your own actions anymore.', 876.171, 879.951, NULL),
  (27687, 136, 'And the result is', 879.951, 881.877, NULL),
  (27688, 136, 'that you are getting disconnected', 881.877, 884.277, NULL),
  (27689, 136, 'with the goals and aspirations 
that once you have set to yourself.', 884.277, 889.062, NULL),
  (27690, 136, 'When the way is filled
with too much doubts,', 889.322, 892.318, NULL),
  (27691, 136, 'more often you will stop
instead of moving on.', 892.318, 896.510, NULL),
  (27692, 136, 'That we know the five hindrances now,', 899.551, 902.585, NULL),
  (27693, 136, 'what are we going to do about them?', 904.032, 906.451, NULL),
  (27694, 136, 'You need to align and structure
your life in such a way', 908.853, 915.153, NULL),
  (27695, 136, 'to prevent those hindrances from arising.', 916.227, 920.676, NULL),
  (27696, 136, 'If you are not successful,', 921.485, 923.925, NULL),
  (27697, 136, 'you need to use techniques
in order to remove them.', 925.946, 930.328, NULL),
  (27698, 136, 'Each of these hindrances is placing
the dark cloud on your mind,', 930.968, 937.883, NULL),
  (27699, 136, 'or on the way of your climb.', 938.008, 940.958, NULL),
  (27700, 136, 'Simply remember one thing:', 942.028, 944.438, NULL),
  (27701, 136, 'Just let it rain.', 946.028, 948.401, NULL),
  (27702, 136, '(Sound of rain)', 948.401, 950.281, NULL),
  (27703, 136, 'This is a four step method', 950.281, 954.623, NULL),
  (27704, 136, 'to help you removing those hindrances.', 955.283, 959.280, NULL),
  (27705, 136, 'The first step is recognize', 959.430, 962.300, NULL),
  (27706, 136, 'in what state of the mind
you are finding yourself in.', 962.300, 966.606, NULL),
  (27707, 136, '[Recognize, Accept,
Investigate, Non-Identity]', 966.606, 969.116, NULL),
  (27708, 136, 'Afterwards, learn to accept, acknowledge,', 969.116, 973.946, NULL),
  (27709, 136, 'and allow the situation or a person', 973.946, 977.936, NULL),
  (27710, 136, 'to be the way how it is,', 978.096, 980.404, NULL),
  (27711, 136, 'to be the way how they are.', 980.404, 983.003, NULL),
  (27712, 136, 'Investigate your
emotional and mental state,', 984.870, 988.290, NULL),
  (27713, 136, 'and ask questions:', 988.290, 989.890, NULL),
  (27714, 136, 'Why did it come up?', 991.785, 993.677, NULL),
  (27715, 136, 'What is going to be the consequence
if I remain in that state?', 994.745, 999.349, NULL),
  (27716, 136, 'And ultimately, non-identification means:', 1001.023, 1004.493, NULL),
  (27717, 136, 'It is the practice.', 1005.086, 1007.426, NULL),
  (27718, 136, 'I am not the body.', 1009.022, 1011.636, NULL),
  (27719, 136, 'I am not the mind.', 1014.714, 1017.519, NULL),
  (27720, 136, 'I am not my emotion.', 1019.328, 1022.255, NULL),
  (27721, 136, 'It''s just that I can see
all these three aspects about me.', 1023.586, 1029.777, NULL),
  (27722, 136, 'All of our lifetimes,', 1037.732, 1039.795, NULL),
  (27723, 136, 'all of our lives are too unique', 1041.919, 1045.219, NULL),
  (27724, 136, 'to copy the path from someone else.', 1046.943, 1051.516, NULL),
  (27725, 136, 'To bring meaning to your life,', 1054.690, 1058.420, NULL),
  (27726, 136, 'to bring value into your life,', 1060.223, 1063.370, NULL),
  (27727, 136, 'you need to learn and master yourself,', 1064.520, 1067.950, NULL),
  (27728, 136, 'and don''t let the hindrances stop you.', 1067.950, 1070.870, NULL),
  (27729, 136, 'If any of you chooses', 1073.116, 1075.774, NULL),
  (27730, 136, 'to climb that path to clarity,', 1076.938, 1080.363, NULL),
  (27731, 136, 'I would be very happy
to meet you at the peak.', 1081.498, 1085.908, NULL),
  (27732, 136, '(Music) (Applause)', 1086.128, 1088.103, NULL),
  (27733, 137, 'Transcriber: Nadine Hennig
Reviewer: Ilze Garda', 0.000, 7.000, NULL),
  (27734, 137, 'When I was growing up, there was this song
we used to sing on the playground,', 5.471, 10.002, NULL),
  (27735, 137, 'and it went like this,', 10.011, 11.772, NULL),
  (27736, 137, '"Tracy and so and so,
sitting in a tree, k-i-s-s-i-n-g,', 11.773, 18.053, NULL),
  (27737, 137, 'first comes love, then comes marriage,', 18.054, 21.279, NULL),
  (27738, 137, 'then comes baby in a baby carriage."', 21.280, 25.031, NULL),
  (27739, 137, 'And I''m like,', 25.811, 26.864, NULL),
  (27740, 137, '"OK, that''s it! That''s how you do life.
That''s how you do a relationship.', 26.865, 32.098, NULL),
  (27741, 137, 'Love, marriage, baby carriage. OK, got it!', 32.100, 35.214, NULL),
  (27742, 137, '(Laughter)', 35.215, 36.804, NULL),
  (27743, 137, 'Then I grew up, and this is
what my life turned out to be.', 36.805, 41.116, NULL),
  (27744, 137, '(Laughter)', 41.119, 43.048, NULL),
  (27745, 137, 'Slightly more complicated, right?
(Laughter)', 43.049, 48.245, NULL),
  (27746, 137, 'Love, marriage, divorce,
dry spells, love, marriage,', 48.246, 54.239, NULL),
  (27747, 137, 'co-parenting, another marriage,
another divorce;', 54.240, 60.051, NULL),
  (27748, 137, 'you got the picture.', 60.052, 61.951, NULL),
  (27749, 137, '(Laughter)', 61.952, 63.931, NULL),
  (27750, 137, '(Applause)', 63.932, 65.464, NULL),
  (27751, 137, 'So if you''re good at math and/or
a fast reader, what you''ve got there', 69.674, 73.446, NULL),
  (27752, 137, 'is that I''ve been married three times.', 73.447, 76.153, NULL),
  (27753, 137, 'Yep, three, and divorced.', 77.023, 80.119, NULL),
  (27754, 137, 'What that is supposed to mean is
that I''m a total failure at relationships.', 80.120, 85.536, NULL),
  (27755, 137, 'And that is one way
to look at it, but not the only way.', 85.539, 89.531, NULL),
  (27756, 137, 'Because what I think really happened
is that I kept marrying the wrong person.', 90.391, 94.750, NULL),
  (27757, 137, 'No, it''s not that I didn''t--
it''s not that I chose bad guys.', 95.563, 98.938, NULL),
  (27758, 137, 'My first two husbands were amazing men', 98.939, 101.169, NULL),
  (27759, 137, 'who are now married
to wonderful women who aren''t me.', 101.170, 104.712, NULL),
  (27760, 137, '(Laughter)', 104.713, 106.292, NULL),
  (27761, 137, 'And my third husband, well,
we''re friends on Facebook now.', 106.293, 111.043, NULL),
  (27762, 137, 'So, all is well that ends well, right?', 111.044, 114.305, NULL),
  (27763, 137, 'After the collapse of
my third marriage in 2005,', 115.365, 118.969, NULL),
  (27764, 137, 'I realized that I''ve been marrying
everyone in sight,', 118.970, 121.989, NULL),
  (27765, 137, 'except the one person
that I really needed to marry', 121.990, 125.171, NULL),
  (27766, 137, 'in order to have a great relationship', 125.172, 127.761, NULL),
  (27767, 137, 'and that once I married that person,', 127.762, 130.158, NULL),
  (27768, 137, 'all of my relationships would be
successes, even the failures.', 130.160, 135.119, NULL),
  (27769, 137, 'The so-called failures, actually.', 135.759, 138.223, NULL),
  (27770, 137, 'Since we''re talking today
about women inventing,', 138.224, 141.078, NULL),
  (27771, 137, 'I''m going to talk about
inventing relationships.', 141.079, 144.611, NULL),
  (27772, 137, 'What I''ve found through a lot of trial
and obviously, many, many, many errors,', 144.612, 150.780, NULL),
  (27773, 137, 'to be the thing that has
transformed my life and love,', 151.511, 155.608, NULL),
  (27774, 137, 'and that is this idea
of marrying yourself.', 155.609, 159.744, NULL),
  (27775, 137, 'So what does it mean to marry yourself?', 161.064, 164.585, NULL),
  (27776, 137, 'It''s a big idea.', 164.586, 165.554, NULL),
  (27777, 137, 'It is as big as marriage itself
except, if I could just summarize it,', 165.555, 170.839, NULL),
  (27778, 137, 'it would be that you enter
into a relationship with yourself', 170.840, 175.372, NULL),
  (27779, 137, 'and then you put a ring on it.', 175.373, 177.966, NULL),
  (27780, 137, '(Laughter)', 177.967, 179.513, NULL),
  (27781, 137, 'In other words,
you commit to yourself fully.', 179.514, 183.644, NULL),
  (27782, 137, 'And then you build
a relationship with yourself', 183.645, 185.932, NULL),
  (27783, 137, 'to the point where you realize
that you''re whole right now,', 185.933, 190.219, NULL),
  (27784, 137, 'that there is no man, woman, job,
circumstance that can happen to you', 190.220, 196.754, NULL),
  (27785, 137, 'that is going to make you more whole
because you already are.', 196.755, 200.981, NULL),
  (27786, 137, 'And this changes your life.', 201.641, 203.500, NULL),
  (27787, 137, 'By now, I''m sure at least
some of you are wondering', 204.730, 207.734, NULL),
  (27788, 137, 'why you should be listening
to a three-time divorcee', 207.735, 210.291, NULL),
  (27789, 137, 'talk about marriage?', 210.292, 211.493, NULL),
  (27790, 137, '(Laughter)', 211.494, 212.430, NULL),
  (27791, 137, 'Even to herself. And I understand that.', 212.431, 216.279, NULL),
  (27792, 137, 'Here''s what I have to say about that:', 216.280, 219.019, NULL),
  (27793, 137, 'what I''ve learned and my experience is', 219.020, 221.912, NULL),
  (27794, 137, 'that the places where you have
the biggest challenges in your life', 221.913, 225.145, NULL),
  (27795, 137, 'become the places where you
have the most to give', 225.146, 228.275, NULL),
  (27796, 137, 'if you do your inner work.', 228.276, 230.113, NULL),
  (27797, 137, 'I kind of want to say that again:', 230.114, 231.695, NULL),
  (27798, 137, 'the places where you have
the biggest challenges', 231.696, 234.111, NULL),
  (27799, 137, 'are the places where you
have the most to give.', 234.112, 237.347, NULL),
  (27800, 137, 'So let me tell you a little bit
about the person I truly needed to marry:', 237.348, 240.862, NULL),
  (27801, 137, 'myself.', 240.863, 241.967, NULL),
  (27802, 137, 'I am from Minneapolis. Wooh!', 242.792, 246.501, NULL),
  (27803, 137, '(Laughter)', 246.513, 248.712, NULL),
  (27804, 137, 'My mom was a prostitute and an alcoholic.', 248.713, 252.427, NULL),
  (27805, 137, 'She put me in foster care
when I was three months old.', 252.428, 255.380, NULL),
  (27806, 137, 'My dad was a criminal;', 255.381, 258.350, NULL),
  (27807, 137, 'he was a drug dealer and a pimp
with a heart of gold', 258.351, 261.776, NULL),
  (27808, 137, '- actually, they both had hearts of gold -', 261.777, 264.266, NULL),
  (27809, 137, 'and he spent more or less
my whole life in prison.', 264.267, 267.767, NULL),
  (27810, 137, 'He just got out of prison
after his most recent sentence', 267.768, 270.709, NULL),
  (27811, 137, 'which was 20 years.', 270.710, 272.184, NULL),
  (27812, 137, 'Until the age of nine, I was probably
in two dozen foster homes.', 274.644, 278.583, NULL),
  (27813, 137, 'The thing you need to know
about this story', 278.584, 280.595, NULL),
  (27814, 137, '- there are a lot of details, obviously -
but the thing you need to know', 280.596, 284.009, NULL),
  (27815, 137, 'is that I came out of that childhood
with one goal: to never be left.', 284.010, 290.269, NULL),
  (27816, 137, 'The way I was going to do that
is that I was going to get married.', 291.387, 295.750, NULL),
  (27817, 137, 'That was the way I was going
to accomplish that goal.', 296.670, 299.830, NULL),
  (27818, 137, 'So I got married the first time
to a guy I met when I was 17.', 299.831, 302.994, NULL),
  (27819, 137, 'We got married a couple
of years later, when I was 19.', 302.995, 305.519, NULL),
  (27820, 137, 'He was a really good guy
from a great family, he had an MBA.', 305.520, 308.621, NULL),
  (27821, 137, 'I mean, it was like,
you know, marriage material.', 308.622, 313.430, NULL),
  (27822, 137, 'You know, I was thrilled.', 316.590, 318.045, NULL),
  (27823, 137, 'I was like, "I have a family.
I belong somewhere. This is wonderful."', 318.046, 322.412, NULL),
  (27824, 137, 'And then after five years I left him.', 322.413, 325.174, NULL),
  (27825, 137, 'Then ten years later, I got married again
to another wonderful guy,', 325.175, 329.789, NULL),
  (27826, 137, 'who is the father of my
now 16-years-old son.', 329.790, 333.393, NULL),
  (27827, 137, 'We still have a wonderful relationship.
He is a really good guy.', 333.394, 336.936, NULL),
  (27828, 137, 'But after four years I left him, too.', 336.937, 339.598, NULL),
  (27829, 137, 'And I am not proud to say that I did that,
but in order to really marry yourself,', 339.599, 343.418, NULL),
  (27830, 137, 'you have to get sometimes
very painfully honest with yourself', 343.419, 346.663, NULL),
  (27831, 137, 'about what it is that you''ve done.', 346.664, 348.973, NULL),
  (27832, 137, 'So I''m not proud of that.', 350.363, 351.719, NULL),
  (27833, 137, 'Then eight years later,
I got married again, when I was 40,', 351.720, 355.250, NULL),
  (27834, 137, 'and I was like, "OK, this feels right!"', 355.251, 358.732, NULL),
  (27835, 137, 'Let me tell you what felt right
to a girl who was in 24 foster homes:', 361.382, 366.557, NULL),
  (27836, 137, 'a guy who started to date
after nine months of marriage;', 367.277, 373.357, NULL),
  (27837, 137, 'essentially, he started dating
a 21-year-old girl.', 373.358, 376.093, NULL),
  (27838, 137, 'OK, I mean, it would be funny,
if it weren''t so tragic.', 377.103, 380.565, NULL),
  (27839, 137, 'You have to have a sense of...
that is why we''re Facebook friends.', 381.505, 385.229, NULL),
  (27840, 137, 'So, here I am looking
at this person that I just described', 385.230, 391.235, NULL),
  (27841, 137, 'with a terrible track record
of relationships,', 391.236, 393.818, NULL),
  (27842, 137, 'and I''m like, "I''m supposed to marry her?', 393.819, 396.282, NULL),
  (27843, 137, 'This is the woman
you want me to marry?"', 396.283, 398.899, NULL),
  (27844, 137, 'And the answer is yes.', 399.659, 401.508, NULL),
  (27845, 137, 'Because here is the deal:', 402.238, 404.194, NULL),
  (27846, 137, 'the thing about marrying yourself
is not just like cohabitating.', 404.195, 407.653, NULL),
  (27847, 137, 'You''re not just going to date
for a while and see how it turns out.', 407.654, 411.267, NULL),
  (27848, 137, 'You are going to do this
till death do you part.', 411.268, 416.082, NULL),
  (27849, 137, 'You are going to take vows.', 416.083, 418.192, NULL),
  (27850, 137, 'So here are the vows.', 419.502, 421.978, NULL),
  (27851, 137, 'Number 1:', 421.979, 423.755, NULL),
  (27852, 137, 'you are going to marry yourself
for richer or for poorer.', 423.756, 426.977, NULL),
  (27853, 137, 'This means you are going
to love yourself right where you are.', 426.978, 431.924, NULL),
  (27854, 137, 'You don''t say to yourself, "When you get
to the corner of Hollywood and Vine,', 431.925, 435.654, NULL),
  (27855, 137, 'then I will marry you."', 435.655, 437.614, NULL),
  (27856, 137, 'You don''t say, "When you lose
ten pounds, then I will love you."', 437.615, 441.621, NULL),
  (27857, 137, 'And you don''t say, "If you hadn''t
married that loser, I would love you,', 442.461, 446.497, NULL),
  (27858, 137, 'but since you did,
I''m sorry, I think it''s over."', 446.498, 449.802, NULL),
  (27859, 137, 'When you marry yourself,
you walk yourself down that aisle', 450.732, 454.980, NULL),
  (27860, 137, 'exactly where you are.', 454.981, 457.270, NULL),
  (27861, 137, 'And paradoxically, I found
that loving myself exactly where I am', 458.070, 462.225, NULL),
  (27862, 137, 'is the only way to get where I am going.', 462.226, 465.472, NULL),
  (27863, 137, 'Number 2:', 466.472, 468.131, NULL),
  (27864, 137, 'you are going to marry yourself
for better or for worse.', 468.132, 471.450, NULL),
  (27865, 137, 'What this means is that most of us
are willing to love ourselves for better,', 472.200, 477.702, NULL),
  (27866, 137, 'I mean, sure, I am having
a great hair day today.', 477.703, 481.502, NULL),
  (27867, 137, 'I love me.', 481.503, 482.473, NULL),
  (27868, 137, '(Laughter)', 482.474, 484.333, NULL),
  (27869, 137, 'That''s not what I am talking about.', 484.334, 486.769, NULL),
  (27870, 137, 'I''m talking about for worse,
you know, the big life disappointments.', 486.770, 490.696, NULL),
  (27871, 137, 'Maybe you don''t own a home,
you didn''t get the career you wanted,', 490.697, 493.759, NULL),
  (27872, 137, 'maybe you didn''t graduate from college,
or get the relationship you wanted.', 493.760, 497.709, NULL),
  (27873, 137, 'Maybe it hasn''t turned out--
maybe you fight with your mum,', 497.710, 500.481, NULL),
  (27874, 137, 'maybe you watch too much reality TV,', 500.482, 502.484, NULL),
  (27875, 137, 'whatever it is, it doesn''t matter anymore.', 502.485, 506.783, NULL),
  (27876, 137, 'Because when you marry yourself,
you agree to stay with you no matter what.', 508.773, 514.501, NULL),
  (27877, 137, 'Third,', 515.712, 517.033, NULL),
  (27878, 137, 'you marry yourself
in sickness and in health.', 517.034, 520.188, NULL),
  (27879, 137, 'What this means is that you forgive
yourself for your mistakes.', 520.190, 524.840, NULL),
  (27880, 137, 'A mistake isn''t actually a failure
unless you don''t learn from it', 525.700, 529.239, NULL),
  (27881, 137, 'and unless you don''t grow.', 529.240, 531.200, NULL),
  (27882, 137, 'There is a saying, "You ask for patience,
and what you get is a line at the bank."', 532.180, 538.510, NULL),
  (27883, 137, '(Laughter)', 538.520, 541.179, NULL),
  (27884, 137, 'What that means is that life
does not give you what you''ve asked for,', 541.180, 544.872, NULL),
  (27885, 137, 'it gives you the people,
places, and situations', 544.873, 547.959, NULL),
  (27886, 137, 'that allow you to develop
what you ask for.', 547.960, 550.605, NULL),
  (27887, 137, 'And the thing is if you don''t get it
right the first time,', 551.445, 554.783, NULL),
  (27888, 137, 'life will give it to you again.', 554.784, 556.393, NULL),
  (27889, 137, '(Laughter)', 556.394, 557.618, NULL),
  (27890, 137, 'Because life is very generous that way.', 557.619, 560.124, NULL),
  (27891, 137, 'It''s like I didn''t get it the first time,
in the first marriage,', 560.125, 563.527, NULL),
  (27892, 137, 'and I didn''t get it the second time,
maybe the third time I''ll get it.', 563.528, 568.899, NULL),
  (27893, 137, 'So inside that terrible experience
of that third marriage,', 570.579, 574.137, NULL),
  (27894, 137, 'I learned something
about "in sickness and in health".', 574.138, 577.340, NULL),
  (27895, 137, 'What I learned is how to sit
by my own bedside,', 577.341, 580.986, NULL),
  (27896, 137, 'and how to hold my own hand,
and how to nurse myself,', 580.987, 584.519, NULL),
  (27897, 137, 'and how to comfort myself.', 584.520, 586.979, NULL),
  (27898, 137, 'What I learned is that I am
a person that I can count on.', 586.980, 591.496, NULL),
  (27899, 137, 'Last but not least, you marry yourself--', 593.156, 596.500, NULL),
  (27900, 137, 'when you marry yourself,
it''s to have and to hold yourself.', 597.900, 602.288, NULL),
  (27901, 137, 'What does it mean to have and to hold?', 603.238, 606.265, NULL),
  (27902, 137, 'Well, I think it means
that you love yourself', 606.266, 609.270, NULL),
  (27903, 137, 'the way you want
someone else to love you.', 609.271, 612.206, NULL),
  (27904, 137, 'I had always been going
through life with this sense of lack.', 614.236, 617.651, NULL),
  (27905, 137, 'I felt like I was kind of half a person,
and that I was missing something.', 617.652, 622.968, NULL),
  (27906, 137, 'I went into my relationships', 623.788, 625.147, NULL),
  (27907, 137, 'hoping to solve this feeling
that I had my entire life:', 625.148, 628.862, NULL),
  (27908, 137, 'that I was not whole
unless someone loved me.', 628.863, 631.332, NULL),
  (27909, 137, 'The truth was', 631.912, 633.447, NULL),
  (27910, 137, 'that I wasn''t ever going to feel whole
until I learned to love myself.', 633.448, 637.297, NULL),
  (27911, 137, 'So this business of marrying yourself
transforms every area of your life:', 638.207, 641.931, NULL),
  (27912, 137, 'your business, family relationships,
kids, social relationships, friends.', 641.932, 647.176, NULL),
  (27913, 137, 'Because when you marry yourself,
this huge thing happens:', 647.177, 649.972, NULL),
  (27914, 137, 'you become able to love
in this whole new way.', 649.973, 652.618, NULL),
  (27915, 137, 'You become able to love other people
right where they are, for who they are,', 652.619, 657.046, NULL),
  (27916, 137, 'the same way you''re already
loving yourself.', 657.047, 659.961, NULL),
  (27917, 137, 'And of course, this is
what the world needs more of.', 661.001, 664.509, NULL),
  (27918, 137, 'So when I married myself, and I realized
that I already had everything I needed,', 664.510, 668.333, NULL),
  (27919, 137, 'I started seeing it as my job', 668.334, 669.936, NULL),
  (27920, 137, 'to basically just light up
my little corner of the world.', 669.937, 673.092, NULL),
  (27921, 137, 'That''s my new job.', 673.842, 675.752, NULL),
  (27922, 137, 'Because I don''t need anything,
I already have it.', 675.752, 678.127, NULL),
  (27923, 137, 'So when I take meetings,', 678.128, 679.275, NULL),
  (27924, 137, 'it''s all about how can I help
this person achieve her goal?', 679.276, 682.577, NULL),
  (27925, 137, 'When I''m in my social communities,', 682.578, 684.219, NULL),
  (27926, 137, 'it is like what can I bring
to this that only I can bring?', 684.220, 687.415, NULL),
  (27927, 137, 'When I go on dates,', 687.416, 688.416, NULL),
  (27928, 137, 'it is like how can I just discover
another person maybe for just one hour', 688.417, 693.366, NULL),
  (27929, 137, 'which, of course, brings me a full circle.', 693.367, 696.035, NULL),
  (27930, 137, 'Because people always asked me
about my love life; they want to know.', 696.995, 700.932, NULL),
  (27931, 137, '(Laughter)', 700.933, 703.496, NULL),
  (27932, 137, 'You know, the answer is,
I am still working on it.', 704.306, 706.693, NULL),
  (27933, 137, 'Aren''t we all?', 706.694, 707.962, NULL),
  (27934, 137, 'So this is where I am right now.', 709.132, 711.248, NULL),
  (27935, 137, 'About three months ago,
I went on a first date.', 711.249, 714.153, NULL),
  (27936, 137, 'About 30 minutes into the date,
I found myself paying attention', 715.123, 720.831, NULL),
  (27937, 137, 'not to whether he liked me,
but how I felt in his presence.', 720.832, 726.743, NULL),
  (27938, 137, 'I noticed that I was light, happy, joking.', 727.933, 731.282, NULL),
  (27939, 137, 'As I reflected on the date afterwards,
I was like, "Wow, I got really excited!', 731.283, 735.719, NULL),
  (27940, 137, 'Look, this is how committed
I am to myself."', 736.439, 739.323, NULL),
  (27941, 137, 'I am not even on this date
trying to get someone to like me.', 739.324, 744.426, NULL),
  (27942, 137, 'I am more interested in how I feel
about me than how he feels about me,', 745.536, 749.211, NULL),
  (27943, 137, 'not because I am selfish,
but because the only relationship', 749.212, 752.101, NULL),
  (27944, 137, 'I am ever going to have
with another person', 752.102, 754.108, NULL),
  (27945, 137, 'is the one that I am
already having with myself -', 754.109, 756.646, NULL),
  (27946, 137, 'just going to have it with them now.', 756.647, 758.816, NULL),
  (27947, 137, 'So it turned out he liked me,
and we are still together.', 759.576, 764.584, NULL),
  (27948, 137, 'It''s cool and amazing,
but I''ve been married three times,', 764.585, 768.429, NULL),
  (27949, 137, 'so slow down!', 768.430, 769.491, NULL),
  (27950, 137, '(Laughter)', 769.492, 771.132, NULL),
  (27951, 137, 'The thing is that I am not trying
to get security from him through marriage,', 773.772, 778.472, NULL),
  (27952, 137, 'and, God forbid, a baby carriage.', 778.473, 781.492, NULL),
  (27953, 137, 'I am only here to
